            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-11082",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "binutils: GNU Binutils Linker heap-based overflow"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A flaw has been found in GNU Binutils 2.45. Impacted is the function _bfd_elf_parse_eh_frame of the file bfd/elf-eh-frame.c of the component Linker. Executing manipulation can lead to heap-based buffer overflow. The attack is restricted to local execution. The exploit has been published and may be used. This patch is called ea1a0737c7692737a644af0486b71e4a392cbca8. A patch should be applied to remediate this issue. The code maintainer replied with \"[f]ixed for 2.46\"."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-11082",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2025-11082\nSeverity: LOW\nPackage: libsframe1\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2025-11082](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-11082)\nA flaw has been found in GNU Binutils 2.45. Impacted is the function _bfd_elf_parse_eh_frame of the file bfd/elf-eh-frame.c of the component Linker. Executing manipulation can lead to heap-based buffer overflow. The attack is restricted to local execution. The exploit has been published and may be used. This patch is called ea1a0737c7692737a644af0486b71e4a392cbca8. A patch should be applied to remediate this issue. The code maintainer replied with \"[f]ixed for 2.46\".",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2025-11082**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|LOW|libsframe1||[CVE-2025-11082](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-11082)|\n\nA flaw has been found in GNU Binutils 2.45. Impacted is the function _bfd_elf_parse_eh_frame of the file bfd/elf-eh-frame.c of the component Linker. Executing manipulation can lead to heap-based buffer overflow. The attack is restricted to local execution. The exploit has been published and may be used. This patch is called ea1a0737c7692737a644af0486b71e4a392cbca8. A patch should be applied to remediate this issue. The code maintainer replied with \"[f]ixed for 2.46\"."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "2.0",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
