            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-69645",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "binutils: Binutils objdump: Denial of Service via crafted DWARF debug information"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Binutils objdump contains a denial-of-service vulnerability when processing a crafted binary with malformed DWARF debug information. A logic error in the handling of DWARF compilation units can result in an invalid offset_size value being used inside byte_get_little_endian, leading to an abort (SIGABRT). The issue was observed in binutils 2.44. A local attacker can trigger the crash by supplying a malicious input file."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-69645",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2025-69645\nSeverity: LOW\nPackage: libsframe1\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2025-69645](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-69645)\nBinutils objdump contains a denial-of-service vulnerability when processing a crafted binary with malformed DWARF debug information. A logic error in the handling of DWARF compilation units can result in an invalid offset_size value being used inside byte_get_little_endian, leading to an abort (SIGABRT). The issue was observed in binutils 2.44. A local attacker can trigger the crash by supplying a malicious input file.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2025-69645**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|LOW|libsframe1||[CVE-2025-69645](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-69645)|\n\nBinutils objdump contains a denial-of-service vulnerability when processing a crafted binary with malformed DWARF debug information. A logic error in the handling of DWARF compilation units can result in an invalid offset_size value being used inside byte_get_little_endian, leading to an abort (SIGABRT). The issue was observed in binutils 2.44. A local attacker can trigger the crash by supplying a malicious input file."
              },
