            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-69649",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "binutils: NULL pointer dereference in readelf via crafted ELF binary with malformed header fields"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "GNU Binutils thru 2.46 readelf contains a null pointer dereference vulnerability when processing a crafted ELF binary with malformed header fields. During relocation processing, an invalid or null section pointer may be passed into display_relocations(), resulting in a segmentation fault (SIGSEGV) and abrupt termination. No evidence of memory corruption beyond the null pointer dereference, nor any possibility of code execution, was observed."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-69649",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2025-69649\nSeverity: LOW\nPackage: libsframe1\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2025-69649](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-69649)\nGNU Binutils thru 2.46 readelf contains a null pointer dereference vulnerability when processing a crafted ELF binary with malformed header fields. During relocation processing, an invalid or null section pointer may be passed into display_relocations(), resulting in a segmentation fault (SIGSEGV) and abrupt termination. No evidence of memory corruption beyond the null pointer dereference, nor any possibility of code execution, was observed.",
