            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-69652",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "binutils: abort in readelf via crafted ELF binary with malformed DWARF abbrev or debug information"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "GNU Binutils thru 2.46 readelf contains a vulnerability that leads to an abort (SIGABRT) when processing a crafted ELF binary with malformed DWARF abbrev or debug information. Due to incomplete state cleanup in process_debug_info(), an invalid debug_info_p state may propagate into DWARF attribute parsing routines. When certain malformed attributes result in an unexpected data length of zero, byte_get_little_endian() triggers a fatal abort. No evidence of memory corruption or code execution was observed; the impact is limited to denial of service."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-69652",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2025-69652\nSeverity: LOW\nPackage: libsframe1\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2025-69652](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-69652)\nGNU Binutils thru 2.46 readelf contains a vulnerability that leads to an abort (SIGABRT) when processing a crafted ELF binary with malformed DWARF abbrev or debug information. Due to incomplete state cleanup in process_debug_info(), an invalid debug_info_p state may propagate into DWARF attribute parsing routines. When certain malformed attributes result in an unexpected data length of zero, byte_get_little_endian() triggers a fatal abort. No evidence of memory corruption or code execution was observed; the impact is limited to denial of service.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2025-69652**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|LOW|libsframe1||[CVE-2025-69652](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-69652)|\n\nGNU Binutils thru 2.46 readelf contains a vulnerability that leads to an abort (SIGABRT) when processing a crafted ELF binary with malformed DWARF abbrev or debug information. Due to incomplete state cleanup in process_debug_info(), an invalid debug_info_p state may propagate into DWARF attribute parsing routines. When certain malformed attributes result in an unexpected data length of zero, byte_get_little_endian() triggers a fatal abort. No evidence of memory corruption or code execution was observed; the impact is limited to denial of service."
              },
