              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "git: The --mirror option for git leaks secret for deleted content, aka the \"GitBleed\""
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The --mirror documentation for Git through 2.35.1 does not mention the availability of deleted content, aka the \"GitBleed\" issue. This could present a security risk if information-disclosure auditing processes rely on a clone operation without the --mirror option. Note: This has been disputed by multiple 3rd parties who believe this is an intended feature of the git binary and does not pose a security risk."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2022-24975",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2022-24975\nSeverity: LOW\nPackage: git-man\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2022-24975](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2022-24975)\nThe --mirror documentation for Git through 2.35.1 does not mention the availability of deleted content, aka the \"GitBleed\" issue. This could present a security risk if information-disclosure auditing processes rely on a clone operation without the --mirror option. Note: This has been disputed by multiple 3rd parties who believe this is an intended feature of the git binary and does not pose a security risk.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2022-24975**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|LOW|git-man||[CVE-2022-24975](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2022-24975)|\n\nThe --mirror documentation for Git through 2.35.1 does not mention the availability of deleted content, aka the \"GitBleed\" issue. This could present a security risk if information-disclosure auditing processes rely on a clone operation without the --mirror option. Note: This has been disputed by multiple 3rd parties who believe this is an intended feature of the git binary and does not pose a security risk."
              },
              "properties": {
