              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "ImageMagick: ImageMagick: Denial of Service via heap buffer over-write in morphology operation with invalid kernel"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "ImageMagick is free and open-source software used for editing and manipulating digital images. In versions prior to 6.9.13-51 and 7.0.1-0 and above prior to 7.1.2-26, an invalid kernel can cause a heap buffer over-write when performing a morphology operation with a user supplied kernel. This issue has been fixed in versions 6.9.13-51 and 7.1.2-26."
