              "id": "CVE-2026-44169",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "mariadb: MariaDB server: Information disclosure of stored routine definitions due to insufficient privilege check"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "MariaDB server is a community developed fork of MySQL server. From versions 11.4.1 to before 11.4.11, 11.8.1 to before 11.8.7, and 12.3.1, a user getting EXECUTE access to a stored routine via a role, could see the routine definition even without SHOW CREATE ROUTINE privilege. This issue has been patched in versions 11.4.11, 11.8.7, and 12.3.2."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
