            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-34544",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "OpenEXR: OpenEXR: Memory corruption and Denial of Service via crafted EXR file processing"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "OpenEXR provides the specification and reference implementation of the EXR file format, an image storage format for the motion picture industry. From version 3.4.0 to before version 3.4.8, a crafted B44 or B44A EXR file can cause an out-of-bounds write in any application that decodes it via exr_decoding_run(). Consequences range from immediate crash (most likely) to corruption of adjacent heap allocations (layout-dependent). This issue has been patched in version 3.4.8."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-34544",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-34544\nSeverity: HIGH\nPackage: libopenexr-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-34544](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-34544)\nOpenEXR provides the specification and reference implementation of the EXR file format, an image storage format for the motion picture industry. From version 3.4.0 to before version 3.4.8, a crafted B44 or B44A EXR file can cause an out-of-bounds write in any application that decodes it via exr_decoding_run(). Consequences range from immediate crash (most likely) to corruption of adjacent heap allocations (layout-dependent). This issue has been patched in version 3.4.8.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-34544**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|HIGH|libopenexr-dev||[CVE-2026-34544](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-34544)|\n\nOpenEXR provides the specification and reference implementation of the EXR file format, an image storage format for the motion picture industry. From version 3.4.0 to before version 3.4.8, a crafted B44 or B44A EXR file can cause an out-of-bounds write in any application that decodes it via exr_decoding_run(). Consequences range from immediate crash (most likely) to corruption of adjacent heap allocations (layout-dependent). This issue has been patched in version 3.4.8."
              },
              "properties": {
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 7.3,
                "cvssv3_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:R/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H",
                "precision": "very-high",
