            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-59186",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "OpenEXR is the reference implementation and specification for the EXR  ..."
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "OpenEXR is the reference implementation and specification for the EXR image format, widely used in the motion picture industry. In versions before 3.2.11, 3.3.0 through 3.3.12, and 3.4.0 through 3.4.13, a crafted tiled EXR can trigger a heap out-of-bounds write on 32-bit/ILP32 builds when read through the public TiledRgbaInputFile RGBA API. The file uses a small 40x40 dataWindow but a 65537x65537 tile size. On ILP32, the Array2D\u003cRgba\u003e tile-conversion buffer size calculation overflows, allocates a much smaller heap buffer, and tile decode writes past that allocation. This issue is fixed in versions 3.2.11, 3.3.13, and 3.4.14."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
