            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-54411",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "linux-pam: Plaintext password recovery via timing discrepancy in pam_userdb module"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Linux-PAM through 1.7.2 contains an observable timing discrepancy (CWE-208) in the pam_userdb module's plaintext-password comparison path in modules/pam_userdb/pam_userdb.c that allows a local or network-adjacent attacker able to repeatedly drive authentication through a calling service to recover the plaintext password of a target account by measuring response-timing differences."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-54411",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-54411\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: libpam0g\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-54411](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-54411)\nLinux-PAM through 1.7.2 contains an observable timing discrepancy (CWE-208) in the pam_userdb module's plaintext-password comparison path in modules/pam_userdb/pam_userdb.c that allows a local or network-adjacent attacker able to repeatedly drive authentication through a calling service to recover the plaintext password of a target account by measuring response-timing differences.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-54411**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|libpam0g||[CVE-2026-54411](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-54411)|\n\nLinux-PAM through 1.7.2 contains an observable timing discrepancy (CWE-208) in the pam_userdb module's plaintext-password comparison path in modules/pam_userdb/pam_userdb.c that allows a local or network-adjacent attacker able to repeatedly drive authentication through a calling service to recover the plaintext password of a target account by measuring response-timing differences."
              },
