            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-6879",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "python: Python: Performance degradation in XML processing due to quadratic time complexity"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "`Element.findall()` and fully-consumed `Element.iterfind()` exhibit `O(n^2)` time complexity when using XPath index predicates (e.g. `[1]`, `[last()]`, `[last()-N]`) on XML documents with many same-tag siblings. `Element.find()` is only affected when the first match is near the end  of the sibling list, such as with `[last()]` or `[last()-N]`;  `.//item[1]` short-circuits after the first match."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-6879",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-6879\nSeverity: LOW\nPackage: python3.13-minimal\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-6879](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-6879)\n`Element.findall()` and fully-consumed `Element.iterfind()` exhibit `O(n^2)` time complexity when using XPath index predicates (e.g. `[1]`, `[last()]`, `[last()-N]`) on XML documents with many same-tag siblings. `Element.find()` is only affected when the first match is near the end  of the sibling list, such as with `[last()]` or `[last()-N]`;  `.//item[1]` short-circuits after the first match.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-6879**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|LOW|python3.13-minimal||[CVE-2026-6879](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-6879)|\n\n`Element.findall()` and fully-consumed `Element.iterfind()` exhibit `O(n^2)` time complexity when using XPath index predicates (e.g. `[1]`, `[last()]`, `[last()-N]`) on XML documents with many same-tag siblings. `Element.find()` is only affected when the first match is near the end  of the sibling list, such as with `[last()]` or `[last()-N]`;  `.//item[1]` short-circuits after the first match."
              },
