            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-50248",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "unbound: Unbound: DNS response policy replacement via hostname spoofing"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In NLnet Labs Unbound 1.7.0 up to and including 1.25.1, when an auth/rpz zone has a configured primary hostname that resolves to BOGUS A/AAAA, it is still considered as a possible XFR endpoint. A malicious actor that can spoof the hostname's A/AAAA record (no valid RRSIG required) becomes the zone's XFR primary and can replaces the entire zone/the resolver's entire response policy."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-50248",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-50248\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: libunbound8\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-50248](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-50248)\nIn NLnet Labs Unbound 1.7.0 up to and including 1.25.1, when an auth/rpz zone has a configured primary hostname that resolves to BOGUS A/AAAA, it is still considered as a possible XFR endpoint. A malicious actor that can spoof the hostname's A/AAAA record (no valid RRSIG required) becomes the zone's XFR primary and can replaces the entire zone/the resolver's entire response policy.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-50248**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|libunbound8||[CVE-2026-50248](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-50248)|\n\nIn NLnet Labs Unbound 1.7.0 up to and including 1.25.1, when an auth/rpz zone has a configured primary hostname that resolves to BOGUS A/AAAA, it is still considered as a possible XFR endpoint. A malicious actor that can spoof the hostname's A/AAAA record (no valid RRSIG required) becomes the zone's XFR primary and can replaces the entire zone/the resolver's entire response policy."
