            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-31493",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: RDMA/efa: Fix use of completion ctx after free"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nRDMA/efa: Fix use of completion ctx after free\n\nOn admin queue completion handling, if the admin command completed with\nerror we print data from the completion context. The issue is that we\nalready freed the completion context in polling/interrupts handler which\nmeans we print data from context in an unknown state (it might be\nalready used again).\nChange the admin submission flow so alloc/dealloc of the context will be\nsymmetric and dealloc will be called after any potential use of the\ncontext."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-31493",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-31493\nSeverity: HIGH\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-31493](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-31493)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nRDMA/efa: Fix use of completion ctx after free\n\nOn admin queue completion handling, if the admin command completed with\nerror we print data from the completion context. The issue is that we\nalready freed the completion context in polling/interrupts handler which\nmeans we print data from context in an unknown state (it might be\nalready used again).\nChange the admin submission flow so alloc/dealloc of the context will be\nsymmetric and dealloc will be called after any potential use of the\ncontext.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-31493**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|HIGH|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-31493](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-31493)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nRDMA/efa: Fix use of completion ctx after free\n\nOn admin queue completion handling, if the admin command completed with\nerror we print data from the completion context. The issue is that we\nalready freed the completion context in polling/interrupts handler which\nmeans we print data from context in an unknown state (it might be\nalready used again).\nChange the admin submission flow so alloc/dealloc of the context will be\nsymmetric and dealloc will be called after any potential use of the\ncontext."
              },
              "properties": {
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 7.8,
                "cvssv3_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H",
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "7.8",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "HIGH"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-31536",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: smb: server: let send_done handle a completion without IB_SEND_SIGNALED"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nsmb: server: let send_done handle a completion without IB_SEND_SIGNALED\n\nWith smbdirect_send_batch processing we likely have requests without\nIB_SEND_SIGNALED, which will be destroyed in the final request\nthat has IB_SEND_SIGNALED set.\n\nIf the connection is broken all requests are signaled\neven without explicit IB_SEND_SIGNALED."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-31536",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-31536\nSeverity: HIGH\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-31536](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-31536)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nsmb: server: let send_done handle a completion without IB_SEND_SIGNALED\n\nWith smbdirect_send_batch processing we likely have requests without\nIB_SEND_SIGNALED, which will be destroyed in the final request\nthat has IB_SEND_SIGNALED set.\n\nIf the connection is broken all requests are signaled\neven without explicit IB_SEND_SIGNALED.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-31536**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|HIGH|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-31536](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-31536)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nsmb: server: let send_done handle a completion without IB_SEND_SIGNALED\n\nWith smbdirect_send_batch processing we likely have requests without\nIB_SEND_SIGNALED, which will be destroyed in the final request\nthat has IB_SEND_SIGNALED set.\n\nIf the connection is broken all requests are signaled\neven without explicit IB_SEND_SIGNALED."
              },
