            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-72098",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: dm-verity: fix buffer overflow in FEC calculation"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndm-verity: fix buffer overflow in FEC calculation\n\nThere's a buffer overflow in dm-verity-fec:\n\nif (neras \u0026\u0026 *neras \u003c= v-\u003efec-\u003eroots)\n\tfio-\u003eerasures[(*neras)++] = i;\n\nThis allows *neras to reach roots + 1 (the post-increment pushes it past\nroots). This value is then passed as no_eras to decode_rs8(). Inside the\nRS decoder (lib/reed_solomon/decode_rs.c:113-121), the erasure locator\npolynomial loop writes lambda[j] where j can reach nroots + 1 — one\nelement past the end of lambda[] (which is sized nroots + 1, valid\nindices 0..nroots). The out-of-bounds write lands on syn[0], corrupting\nthe syndrome buffer."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-72098",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-72098\nSeverity: HIGH\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-72098](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-72098)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndm-verity: fix buffer overflow in FEC calculation\n\nThere's a buffer overflow in dm-verity-fec:\n\nif (neras \u0026\u0026 *neras \u003c= v-\u003efec-\u003eroots)\n\tfio-\u003eerasures[(*neras)++] = i;\n\nThis allows *neras to reach roots + 1 (the post-increment pushes it past\nroots). This value is then passed as no_eras to decode_rs8(). Inside the\nRS decoder (lib/reed_solomon/decode_rs.c:113-121), the erasure locator\npolynomial loop writes lambda[j] where j can reach nroots + 1 — one\nelement past the end of lambda[] (which is sized nroots + 1, valid\nindices 0..nroots). The out-of-bounds write lands on syn[0], corrupting\nthe syndrome buffer.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-72098**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|HIGH|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-72098](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-72098)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndm-verity: fix buffer overflow in FEC calculation\n\nThere's a buffer overflow in dm-verity-fec:\n\nif (neras \u0026\u0026 *neras \u003c= v-\u003efec-\u003eroots)\n\tfio-\u003eerasures[(*neras)++] = i;\n\nThis allows *neras to reach roots + 1 (the post-increment pushes it past\nroots). This value is then passed as no_eras to decode_rs8(). Inside the\nRS decoder (lib/reed_solomon/decode_rs.c:113-121), the erasure locator\npolynomial loop writes lambda[j] where j can reach nroots + 1 — one\nelement past the end of lambda[] (which is sized nroots + 1, valid\nindices 0..nroots). The out-of-bounds write lands on syn[0], corrupting\nthe syndrome buffer."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "8.0",
