            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-40158",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: ipv6: use RCU in ip6_output()"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nipv6: use RCU in ip6_output()\n\nUse RCU in ip6_output() in order to use dst_dev_rcu() to prevent\npossible UAF.\n\nWe can remove rcu_read_lock()/rcu_read_unlock() pairs\nfrom ip6_finish_output2()."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-40158",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2025-40158\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2025-40158](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-40158)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nipv6: use RCU in ip6_output()\n\nUse RCU in ip6_output() in order to use dst_dev_rcu() to prevent\npossible UAF.\n\nWe can remove rcu_read_lock()/rcu_read_unlock() pairs\nfrom ip6_finish_output2().",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2025-40158**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2025-40158](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-40158)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nipv6: use RCU in ip6_output()\n\nUse RCU in ip6_output() in order to use dst_dev_rcu() to prevent\npossible UAF.\n\nWe can remove rcu_read_lock()/rcu_read_unlock() pairs\nfrom ip6_finish_output2()."
              },
