            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-40168",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: smc: Use __sk_dst_get() and dst_dev_rcu() in smc_clc_prfx_match()"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nsmc: Use __sk_dst_get() and dst_dev_rcu() in smc_clc_prfx_match().\n\nsmc_clc_prfx_match() is called from smc_listen_work() and\nnot under RCU nor RTNL.\n\nUsing sk_dst_get(sk)-\u003edev could trigger UAF.\n\nLet's use __sk_dst_get() and dst_dev_rcu().\n\nNote that the returned value of smc_clc_prfx_match() is not\nused in the caller."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-40168",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2025-40168\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2025-40168](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-40168)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nsmc: Use __sk_dst_get() and dst_dev_rcu() in smc_clc_prfx_match().\n\nsmc_clc_prfx_match() is called from smc_listen_work() and\nnot under RCU nor RTNL.\n\nUsing sk_dst_get(sk)-\u003edev could trigger UAF.\n\nLet's use __sk_dst_get() and dst_dev_rcu().\n\nNote that the returned value of smc_clc_prfx_match() is not\nused in the caller.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2025-40168**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2025-40168](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-40168)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nsmc: Use __sk_dst_get() and dst_dev_rcu() in smc_clc_prfx_match().\n\nsmc_clc_prfx_match() is called from smc_listen_work() and\nnot under RCU nor RTNL.\n\nUsing sk_dst_get(sk)-\u003edev could trigger UAF.\n\nLet's use __sk_dst_get() and dst_dev_rcu().\n\nNote that the returned value of smc_clc_prfx_match() is not\nused in the caller."
              },
