            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-71141",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: drm/tilcdc: Fix removal actions in case of failed probe"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndrm/tilcdc: Fix removal actions in case of failed probe\n\nThe drm_kms_helper_poll_fini() and drm_atomic_helper_shutdown() helpers\nshould only be called when the device has been successfully registered.\nCurrently, these functions are called unconditionally in tilcdc_fini(),\nwhich causes warnings during probe deferral scenarios.\n\n[    7.972317] WARNING: CPU: 0 PID: 23 at drivers/gpu/drm/drm_atomic_state_helper.c:175 drm_atomic_helper_crtc_duplicate_state+0x60/0x68\n...\n[    8.005820]  drm_atomic_helper_crtc_duplicate_state from drm_atomic_get_crtc_state+0x68/0x108\n[    8.005858]  drm_atomic_get_crtc_state from drm_atomic_helper_disable_all+0x90/0x1c8\n[    8.005885]  drm_atomic_helper_disable_all from drm_atomic_helper_shutdown+0x90/0x144\n[    8.005911]  drm_atomic_helper_shutdown from tilcdc_fini+0x68/0xf8 [tilcdc]\n[    8.005957]  tilcdc_fini [tilcdc] from tilcdc_pdev_probe+0xb0/0x6d4 [tilcdc]\n\nFix this by rewriting the failed probe cleanup path using the standard\ngoto error handling pattern, which ensures that cleanup functions are\nonly called on successfully initialized resources. Additionally, remove\nthe now-unnecessary is_registered flag."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-71141",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2025-71141\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2025-71141](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-71141)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndrm/tilcdc: Fix removal actions in case of failed probe\n\nThe drm_kms_helper_poll_fini() and drm_atomic_helper_shutdown() helpers\nshould only be called when the device has been successfully registered.\nCurrently, these functions are called unconditionally in tilcdc_fini(),\nwhich causes warnings during probe deferral scenarios.\n\n[    7.972317] WARNING: CPU: 0 PID: 23 at drivers/gpu/drm/drm_atomic_state_helper.c:175 drm_atomic_helper_crtc_duplicate_state+0x60/0x68\n...\n[    8.005820]  drm_atomic_helper_crtc_duplicate_state from drm_atomic_get_crtc_state+0x68/0x108\n[    8.005858]  drm_atomic_get_crtc_state from drm_atomic_helper_disable_all+0x90/0x1c8\n[    8.005885]  drm_atomic_helper_disable_all from drm_atomic_helper_shutdown+0x90/0x144\n[    8.005911]  drm_atomic_helper_shutdown from tilcdc_fini+0x68/0xf8 [tilcdc]\n[    8.005957]  tilcdc_fini [tilcdc] from tilcdc_pdev_probe+0xb0/0x6d4 [tilcdc]\n\nFix this by rewriting the failed probe cleanup path using the standard\ngoto error handling pattern, which ensures that cleanup functions are\nonly called on successfully initialized resources. Additionally, remove\nthe now-unnecessary is_registered flag.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2025-71141**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2025-71141](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-71141)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndrm/tilcdc: Fix removal actions in case of failed probe\n\nThe drm_kms_helper_poll_fini() and drm_atomic_helper_shutdown() helpers\nshould only be called when the device has been successfully registered.\nCurrently, these functions are called unconditionally in tilcdc_fini(),\nwhich causes warnings during probe deferral scenarios.\n\n[    7.972317] WARNING: CPU: 0 PID: 23 at drivers/gpu/drm/drm_atomic_state_helper.c:175 drm_atomic_helper_crtc_duplicate_state+0x60/0x68\n...\n[    8.005820]  drm_atomic_helper_crtc_duplicate_state from drm_atomic_get_crtc_state+0x68/0x108\n[    8.005858]  drm_atomic_get_crtc_state from drm_atomic_helper_disable_all+0x90/0x1c8\n[    8.005885]  drm_atomic_helper_disable_all from drm_atomic_helper_shutdown+0x90/0x144\n[    8.005911]  drm_atomic_helper_shutdown from tilcdc_fini+0x68/0xf8 [tilcdc]\n[    8.005957]  tilcdc_fini [tilcdc] from tilcdc_pdev_probe+0xb0/0x6d4 [tilcdc]\n\nFix this by rewriting the failed probe cleanup path using the standard\ngoto error handling pattern, which ensures that cleanup functions are\nonly called on successfully initialized resources. Additionally, remove\nthe now-unnecessary is_registered flag."
              },
              "properties": {
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 5.5,
                "cvssv3_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H",
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-71188",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: dmaengine: lpc18xx-dmamux: fix device leak on route allocation"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndmaengine: lpc18xx-dmamux: fix device leak on route allocation\n\nMake sure to drop the reference taken when looking up the DMA mux\nplatform device during route allocation.\n\nNote that holding a reference to a device does not prevent its driver\ndata from going away so there is no point in keeping the reference."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-71188",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2025-71188\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2025-71188](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-71188)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndmaengine: lpc18xx-dmamux: fix device leak on route allocation\n\nMake sure to drop the reference taken when looking up the DMA mux\nplatform device during route allocation.\n\nNote that holding a reference to a device does not prevent its driver\ndata from going away so there is no point in keeping the reference.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2025-71188**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2025-71188](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-71188)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndmaengine: lpc18xx-dmamux: fix device leak on route allocation\n\nMake sure to drop the reference taken when looking up the DMA mux\nplatform device during route allocation.\n\nNote that holding a reference to a device does not prevent its driver\ndata from going away so there is no point in keeping the reference."
              },
              "properties": {
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 5.5,
                "cvssv3_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H",
