            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-71313",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: PCI: endpoint: Add missing NULL check for alloc_workqueue()"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nPCI: endpoint: Add missing NULL check for alloc_workqueue()\n\nalloc_workqueue() can return NULL on memory allocation failure. Without\nproper error checking, this may lead to a NULL pointer dereference when\nqueue_work() is later called with the NULL workqueue pointer in\nepf_ntb_epc_init().\n\nAdd a NULL check immediately after alloc_workqueue() and return -ENOMEM on\nfailure to prevent the driver from loading with an invalid workqueue\npointer."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-71313",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2025-71313\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2025-71313](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-71313)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nPCI: endpoint: Add missing NULL check for alloc_workqueue()\n\nalloc_workqueue() can return NULL on memory allocation failure. Without\nproper error checking, this may lead to a NULL pointer dereference when\nqueue_work() is later called with the NULL workqueue pointer in\nepf_ntb_epc_init().\n\nAdd a NULL check immediately after alloc_workqueue() and return -ENOMEM on\nfailure to prevent the driver from loading with an invalid workqueue\npointer.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2025-71313**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2025-71313](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-71313)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nPCI: endpoint: Add missing NULL check for alloc_workqueue()\n\nalloc_workqueue() can return NULL on memory allocation failure. Without\nproper error checking, this may lead to a NULL pointer dereference when\nqueue_work() is later called with the NULL workqueue pointer in\nepf_ntb_epc_init().\n\nAdd a NULL check immediately after alloc_workqueue() and return -ENOMEM on\nfailure to prevent the driver from loading with an invalid workqueue\npointer."
              },
              "properties": {
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 5.5,
                "cvssv3_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H",
