            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-31692",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: rtnetlink: add missing netlink_ns_capable() check for peer netns"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nrtnetlink: add missing netlink_ns_capable() check for peer netns\n\nrtnl_newlink() lacks a CAP_NET_ADMIN capability check on the peer\nnetwork namespace when creating paired devices (veth, vxcan,\nnetkit). This allows an unprivileged user with a user namespace\nto create interfaces in arbitrary network namespaces, including\ninit_net.\n\nAdd a netlink_ns_capable() check for CAP_NET_ADMIN in the peer\nnamespace before allowing device creation to proceed."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-31692",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-31692\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-31692](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-31692)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nrtnetlink: add missing netlink_ns_capable() check for peer netns\n\nrtnl_newlink() lacks a CAP_NET_ADMIN capability check on the peer\nnetwork namespace when creating paired devices (veth, vxcan,\nnetkit). This allows an unprivileged user with a user namespace\nto create interfaces in arbitrary network namespaces, including\ninit_net.\n\nAdd a netlink_ns_capable() check for CAP_NET_ADMIN in the peer\nnamespace before allowing device creation to proceed.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-31692**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-31692](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-31692)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nrtnetlink: add missing netlink_ns_capable() check for peer netns\n\nrtnl_newlink() lacks a CAP_NET_ADMIN capability check on the peer\nnetwork namespace when creating paired devices (veth, vxcan,\nnetkit). This allows an unprivileged user with a user namespace\nto create interfaces in arbitrary network namespaces, including\ninit_net.\n\nAdd a netlink_ns_capable() check for CAP_NET_ADMIN in the peer\nnamespace before allowing device creation to proceed."
              },
              "properties": {
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 5.5,
                "cvssv3_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H",
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
