            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-43443",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: ASoC: amd: acp-mach-common: Add missing error check for clock acquisition"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nASoC: amd: acp-mach-common: Add missing error check for clock acquisition\n\nThe acp_card_rt5682_init() and acp_card_rt5682s_init() functions did not\ncheck the return values of clk_get(). This could lead to a kernel crash\nwhen the invalid pointers are later dereferenced by clock core\nfunctions.\n\nFix this by:\n1. Changing clk_get() to the device-managed devm_clk_get().\n2. Adding IS_ERR() checks immediately after each clock acquisition."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-43443",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-43443\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-43443](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-43443)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nASoC: amd: acp-mach-common: Add missing error check for clock acquisition\n\nThe acp_card_rt5682_init() and acp_card_rt5682s_init() functions did not\ncheck the return values of clk_get(). This could lead to a kernel crash\nwhen the invalid pointers are later dereferenced by clock core\nfunctions.\n\nFix this by:\n1. Changing clk_get() to the device-managed devm_clk_get().\n2. Adding IS_ERR() checks immediately after each clock acquisition.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-43443**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-43443](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-43443)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nASoC: amd: acp-mach-common: Add missing error check for clock acquisition\n\nThe acp_card_rt5682_init() and acp_card_rt5682s_init() functions did not\ncheck the return values of clk_get(). This could lead to a kernel crash\nwhen the invalid pointers are later dereferenced by clock core\nfunctions.\n\nFix this by:\n1. Changing clk_get() to the device-managed devm_clk_get().\n2. Adding IS_ERR() checks immediately after each clock acquisition."
              },
              "properties": {
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 5.5,
                "cvssv3_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H",
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-43463",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: rxrpc, afs: Fix missing error pointer check after rxrpc_kernel_lookup_peer()"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nrxrpc, afs: Fix missing error pointer check after rxrpc_kernel_lookup_peer()\n\nrxrpc_kernel_lookup_peer() can also return error pointers in addition to\nNULL, so just checking for NULL is not sufficient.\n\nFix this by:\n\n (1) Changing rxrpc_kernel_lookup_peer() to return -ENOMEM rather than NULL\n     on allocation failure.\n\n (2) Making the callers in afs use IS_ERR() and PTR_ERR() to pass on the\n     error code returned."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-43463",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-43463\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-43463](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-43463)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nrxrpc, afs: Fix missing error pointer check after rxrpc_kernel_lookup_peer()\n\nrxrpc_kernel_lookup_peer() can also return error pointers in addition to\nNULL, so just checking for NULL is not sufficient.\n\nFix this by:\n\n (1) Changing rxrpc_kernel_lookup_peer() to return -ENOMEM rather than NULL\n     on allocation failure.\n\n (2) Making the callers in afs use IS_ERR() and PTR_ERR() to pass on the\n     error code returned.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-43463**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-43463](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-43463)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nrxrpc, afs: Fix missing error pointer check after rxrpc_kernel_lookup_peer()\n\nrxrpc_kernel_lookup_peer() can also return error pointers in addition to\nNULL, so just checking for NULL is not sufficient.\n\nFix this by:\n\n (1) Changing rxrpc_kernel_lookup_peer() to return -ENOMEM rather than NULL\n     on allocation failure.\n\n (2) Making the callers in afs use IS_ERR() and PTR_ERR() to pass on the\n     error code returned."
              },
              "properties": {
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 5.5,
                "cvssv3_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H",
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
