            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-46314",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: drm/v3d: Reject empty multisync extension to prevent infinite loop"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndrm/v3d: Reject empty multisync extension to prevent infinite loop\n\nv3d_get_extensions() walks a userspace-provided singly-linked list of\nioctl extensions without any bound on the chain length. A local user\ncan craft a self-referential extension (ext-\u003enext == \u0026ext) with zero\nin_sync_count and out_sync_count, which bypasses the existing duplicate-\nextension guard:\n\n    if (se-\u003ein_sync_count || se-\u003eout_sync_count)\n            return -EINVAL;\n\nThe guard never fires because v3d_get_multisync_post_deps() returns\nimmediately when count is zero, leaving both fields at zero on every\niteration. The result is an infinite loop in kernel context, blocking\nthe calling thread and pegging a CPU core indefinitely.\n\nFix this by rejecting a multisync extension where both in_sync_count\nand out_sync_count are zero in v3d_get_multisync_submit_deps(). An\nempty multisync carries no synchronization information and serves no\nuseful purpose, so returning -EINVAL for such an extension is the\ncorrect defense against this attack vector."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-46314",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-46314\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-46314](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-46314)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndrm/v3d: Reject empty multisync extension to prevent infinite loop\n\nv3d_get_extensions() walks a userspace-provided singly-linked list of\nioctl extensions without any bound on the chain length. A local user\ncan craft a self-referential extension (ext-\u003enext == \u0026ext) with zero\nin_sync_count and out_sync_count, which bypasses the existing duplicate-\nextension guard:\n\n    if (se-\u003ein_sync_count || se-\u003eout_sync_count)\n            return -EINVAL;\n\nThe guard never fires because v3d_get_multisync_post_deps() returns\nimmediately when count is zero, leaving both fields at zero on every\niteration. The result is an infinite loop in kernel context, blocking\nthe calling thread and pegging a CPU core indefinitely.\n\nFix this by rejecting a multisync extension where both in_sync_count\nand out_sync_count are zero in v3d_get_multisync_submit_deps(). An\nempty multisync carries no synchronization information and serves no\nuseful purpose, so returning -EINVAL for such an extension is the\ncorrect defense against this attack vector.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-46314**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-46314](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-46314)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndrm/v3d: Reject empty multisync extension to prevent infinite loop\n\nv3d_get_extensions() walks a userspace-provided singly-linked list of\nioctl extensions without any bound on the chain length. A local user\ncan craft a self-referential extension (ext-\u003enext == \u0026ext) with zero\nin_sync_count and out_sync_count, which bypasses the existing duplicate-\nextension guard:\n\n    if (se-\u003ein_sync_count || se-\u003eout_sync_count)\n            return -EINVAL;\n\nThe guard never fires because v3d_get_multisync_post_deps() returns\nimmediately when count is zero, leaving both fields at zero on every\niteration. The result is an infinite loop in kernel context, blocking\nthe calling thread and pegging a CPU core indefinitely.\n\nFix this by rejecting a multisync extension where both in_sync_count\nand out_sync_count are zero in v3d_get_multisync_submit_deps(). An\nempty multisync carries no synchronization information and serves no\nuseful purpose, so returning -EINVAL for such an extension is the\ncorrect defense against this attack vector."
              },
              "properties": {
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 5.5,
                "cvssv3_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H",
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
