              "id": "CVE-2026-64066",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: netfs: Fix netfs_read_to_pagecache() to pause on subreq failure"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnetfs: Fix netfs_read_to_pagecache() to pause on subreq failure\n\nFix netfs_read_to_pagecache() so that it pauses the generation of new\nsubrequests if an already-issued subrequest fails."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-64066",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-64066\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-64066](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-64066)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnetfs: Fix netfs_read_to_pagecache() to pause on subreq failure\n\nFix netfs_read_to_pagecache() so that it pauses the generation of new\nsubrequests if an already-issued subrequest fails.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-64066**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-64066](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-64066)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnetfs: Fix netfs_read_to_pagecache() to pause on subreq failure\n\nFix netfs_read_to_pagecache() so that it pauses the generation of new\nsubrequests if an already-issued subrequest fails."
              },
