            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-64078",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: netfilter: x_tables: add and use xtables_unregister_table_exit"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnetfilter: x_tables: add and use xtables_unregister_table_exit\n\nPrevious change added xtables_unregister_table_pre_exit to detach the\ntable from the packetpath and to unlink it from the active table list.\nIn case of rmmod, userspace that is doing set/getsockopt for this table\nwill not be able to re-instantiate the table:\n 1. The larval table has been removed already\n 2. existing instantiated table is no longer on the xt pernet table list.\n\nThis adds the second stage helper:\n\nunlink the table from the dying list, free the hook ops (if any) and do\nthe audit notification.  It replaces xt_unregister_table()."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-64078",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-64078\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-64078](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-64078)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnetfilter: x_tables: add and use xtables_unregister_table_exit\n\nPrevious change added xtables_unregister_table_pre_exit to detach the\ntable from the packetpath and to unlink it from the active table list.\nIn case of rmmod, userspace that is doing set/getsockopt for this table\nwill not be able to re-instantiate the table:\n 1. The larval table has been removed already\n 2. existing instantiated table is no longer on the xt pernet table list.\n\nThis adds the second stage helper:\n\nunlink the table from the dying list, free the hook ops (if any) and do\nthe audit notification.  It replaces xt_unregister_table().",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-64078**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-64078](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-64078)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnetfilter: x_tables: add and use xtables_unregister_table_exit\n\nPrevious change added xtables_unregister_table_pre_exit to detach the\ntable from the packetpath and to unlink it from the active table list.\nIn case of rmmod, userspace that is doing set/getsockopt for this table\nwill not be able to re-instantiate the table:\n 1. The larval table has been removed already\n 2. existing instantiated table is no longer on the xt pernet table list.\n\nThis adds the second stage helper:\n\nunlink the table from the dying list, free the hook ops (if any) and do\nthe audit notification.  It replaces xt_unregister_table()."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
