            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-64216",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: Kernel: netfs Use-After-Free vulnerability allows local denial of service and memory corruption"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnetfs: Fix potential UAF in netfs_unlock_abandoned_read_pages()\n\nnetfs_unlock_abandoned_read_pages(rreq) accesses the index of the folios it\nis wanting to unlock and compares that to rreq-\u003eno_unlock_folio so that it\ndoesn't unlock a folio being read for netfs_perform_write() or\nnetfs_write_begin().\n\nHowever, given that netfs_unlock_abandoned_read_pages() is called _after_\nNETFS_RREQ_IN_PROGRESS is cleared, the one folio that it's not allowed to\ndereference is the one specified by -\u003eno_unlock_folio as ownership\nimmediately reverts to the caller.\n\nFix this by storing the folio pointer instead and using that rather than\nthe index.  Also fix netfs_unlock_read_folio() where the same applies."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-64216",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-64216\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: 6.12.107-1\nLink: [CVE-2026-64216](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-64216)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnetfs: Fix potential UAF in netfs_unlock_abandoned_read_pages()\n\nnetfs_unlock_abandoned_read_pages(rreq) accesses the index of the folios it\nis wanting to unlock and compares that to rreq-\u003eno_unlock_folio so that it\ndoesn't unlock a folio being read for netfs_perform_write() or\nnetfs_write_begin().\n\nHowever, given that netfs_unlock_abandoned_read_pages() is called _after_\nNETFS_RREQ_IN_PROGRESS is cleared, the one folio that it's not allowed to\ndereference is the one specified by -\u003eno_unlock_folio as ownership\nimmediately reverts to the caller.\n\nFix this by storing the folio pointer instead and using that rather than\nthe index.  Also fix netfs_unlock_read_folio() where the same applies.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-64216**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev|6.12.107-1|[CVE-2026-64216](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-64216)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnetfs: Fix potential UAF in netfs_unlock_abandoned_read_pages()\n\nnetfs_unlock_abandoned_read_pages(rreq) accesses the index of the folios it\nis wanting to unlock and compares that to rreq-\u003eno_unlock_folio so that it\ndoesn't unlock a folio being read for netfs_perform_write() or\nnetfs_write_begin().\n\nHowever, given that netfs_unlock_abandoned_read_pages() is called _after_\nNETFS_RREQ_IN_PROGRESS is cleared, the one folio that it's not allowed to\ndereference is the one specified by -\u003eno_unlock_folio as ownership\nimmediately reverts to the caller.\n\nFix this by storing the folio pointer instead and using that rather than\nthe index.  Also fix netfs_unlock_read_folio() where the same applies."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-64255",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: wifi: iwlwifi: mld: validate sta_mask before ffs() in BA session handlers"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: iwlwifi: mld: validate sta_mask before ffs() in BA session handlers\n\nThree BA session handlers use ffs(ba_data-\u003esta_mask) - 1 to derive a\nstation ID without checking that sta_mask is non-zero. When sta_mask is\nzero, ffs() returns 0 and the subtraction wraps to 0xFFFFFFFF, causing\nan out-of-bounds access on fw_id_to_link_sta[].\n\nAdd WARN_ON_ONCE(!ba_data-\u003esta_mask) guards before each ffs() call,\nconsistent with the existing check in iwl_mld_ampdu_rx_start()."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-64255",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-64255\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-64255](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-64255)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: iwlwifi: mld: validate sta_mask before ffs() in BA session handlers\n\nThree BA session handlers use ffs(ba_data-\u003esta_mask) - 1 to derive a\nstation ID without checking that sta_mask is non-zero. When sta_mask is\nzero, ffs() returns 0 and the subtraction wraps to 0xFFFFFFFF, causing\nan out-of-bounds access on fw_id_to_link_sta[].\n\nAdd WARN_ON_ONCE(!ba_data-\u003esta_mask) guards before each ffs() call,\nconsistent with the existing check in iwl_mld_ampdu_rx_start().",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-64255**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-64255](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-64255)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: iwlwifi: mld: validate sta_mask before ffs() in BA session handlers\n\nThree BA session handlers use ffs(ba_data-\u003esta_mask) - 1 to derive a\nstation ID without checking that sta_mask is non-zero. When sta_mask is\nzero, ffs() returns 0 and the subtraction wraps to 0xFFFFFFFF, causing\nan out-of-bounds access on fw_id_to_link_sta[].\n\nAdd WARN_ON_ONCE(!ba_data-\u003esta_mask) guards before each ffs() call,\nconsistent with the existing check in iwl_mld_ampdu_rx_start()."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-64389",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: ksmbd: validate NTLMv2 response before updating session key"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nksmbd: validate NTLMv2 response before updating session key\n\nksmbd_auth_ntlmv2() derives the NTLMv2 session key into\nsess-\u003esess_key before it verifies the NTLMv2 response.\nksmbd_decode_ntlmssp_auth_blob() then continues into KEY_XCH even\nwhen ksmbd_auth_ntlmv2() failed.\n\nWith SMB3 multichannel binding, the failed authentication operates on\nan existing session and the session setup error path does not expire\nbinding sessions. A client can send a binding session setup with a\nbad NT proof and KEY_XCH and still modify sess-\u003esess_key before\nSTATUS_LOGON_FAILURE is returned.\n\nRelevant path:\n\n  smb2_sess_setup()\n    -\u003e conn-\u003ebinding = true\n    -\u003e ntlm_authenticate()\n       -\u003e session_user()\n       -\u003e ksmbd_decode_ntlmssp_auth_blob()\n          -\u003e ksmbd_auth_ntlmv2()\n             -\u003e calc_ntlmv2_hash()\n             -\u003e hmac_md5_usingrawkey(..., sess-\u003esess_key)\n             -\u003e crypto_memneq() returns mismatch\n          -\u003e KEY_XCH arc4_crypt(..., sess-\u003esess_key, ...)\n    -\u003e out_err without expiring the binding session\n\nDerive the base session key into a local buffer and copy it to\nsess-\u003esess_key only after the proof matches. Return immediately on\nauthentication failure so KEY_XCH is only processed after successful\nauthentication."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-64389",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-64389\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-64389](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-64389)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nksmbd: validate NTLMv2 response before updating session key\n\nksmbd_auth_ntlmv2() derives the NTLMv2 session key into\nsess-\u003esess_key before it verifies the NTLMv2 response.\nksmbd_decode_ntlmssp_auth_blob() then continues into KEY_XCH even\nwhen ksmbd_auth_ntlmv2() failed.\n\nWith SMB3 multichannel binding, the failed authentication operates on\nan existing session and the session setup error path does not expire\nbinding sessions. A client can send a binding session setup with a\nbad NT proof and KEY_XCH and still modify sess-\u003esess_key before\nSTATUS_LOGON_FAILURE is returned.\n\nRelevant path:\n\n  smb2_sess_setup()\n    -\u003e conn-\u003ebinding = true\n    -\u003e ntlm_authenticate()\n       -\u003e session_user()\n       -\u003e ksmbd_decode_ntlmssp_auth_blob()\n          -\u003e ksmbd_auth_ntlmv2()\n             -\u003e calc_ntlmv2_hash()\n             -\u003e hmac_md5_usingrawkey(..., sess-\u003esess_key)\n             -\u003e crypto_memneq() returns mismatch\n          -\u003e KEY_XCH arc4_crypt(..., sess-\u003esess_key, ...)\n    -\u003e out_err without expiring the binding session\n\nDerive the base session key into a local buffer and copy it to\nsess-\u003esess_key only after the proof matches. Return immediately on\nauthentication failure so KEY_XCH is only processed after successful\nauthentication.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-64389**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-64389](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-64389)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nksmbd: validate NTLMv2 response before updating session key\n\nksmbd_auth_ntlmv2() derives the NTLMv2 session key into\nsess-\u003esess_key before it verifies the NTLMv2 response.\nksmbd_decode_ntlmssp_auth_blob() then continues into KEY_XCH even\nwhen ksmbd_auth_ntlmv2() failed.\n\nWith SMB3 multichannel binding, the failed authentication operates on\nan existing session and the session setup error path does not expire\nbinding sessions. A client can send a binding session setup with a\nbad NT proof and KEY_XCH and still modify sess-\u003esess_key before\nSTATUS_LOGON_FAILURE is returned.\n\nRelevant path:\n\n  smb2_sess_setup()\n    -\u003e conn-\u003ebinding = true\n    -\u003e ntlm_authenticate()\n       -\u003e session_user()\n       -\u003e ksmbd_decode_ntlmssp_auth_blob()\n          -\u003e ksmbd_auth_ntlmv2()\n             -\u003e calc_ntlmv2_hash()\n             -\u003e hmac_md5_usingrawkey(..., sess-\u003esess_key)\n             -\u003e crypto_memneq() returns mismatch\n          -\u003e KEY_XCH arc4_crypt(..., sess-\u003esess_key, ...)\n    -\u003e out_err without expiring the binding session\n\nDerive the base session key into a local buffer and copy it to\nsess-\u003esess_key only after the proof matches. Return immediately on\nauthentication failure so KEY_XCH is only processed after successful\nauthentication."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
