            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-68253",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: drm/i915/hdcp: check streams[] bounds before overflow"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndrm/i915/hdcp: check streams[] bounds before overflow\n\nThe data-\u003estreams[] overflow check is done after the buffer overflow has\nalready happened. Move the overflow check before the write.\n\nSide note, emitting a warning splat with a backtrace might be overkill\nhere, but prefer not changing the behaviour other than not doing the\noverrun.\n\nDiscovered using AI-assisted static analysis confirmed by Intel Product\nSecurity.\n\n(cherry picked from commit 9284ab3b6e776c315883ac2611283d263c9460fd)"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-68253",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-68253\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: 6.12.105-1\nLink: [CVE-2026-68253](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-68253)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndrm/i915/hdcp: check streams[] bounds before overflow\n\nThe data-\u003estreams[] overflow check is done after the buffer overflow has\nalready happened. Move the overflow check before the write.\n\nSide note, emitting a warning splat with a backtrace might be overkill\nhere, but prefer not changing the behaviour other than not doing the\noverrun.\n\nDiscovered using AI-assisted static analysis confirmed by Intel Product\nSecurity.\n\n(cherry picked from commit 9284ab3b6e776c315883ac2611283d263c9460fd)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-68253**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev|6.12.105-1|[CVE-2026-68253](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-68253)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndrm/i915/hdcp: check streams[] bounds before overflow\n\nThe data-\u003estreams[] overflow check is done after the buffer overflow has\nalready happened. Move the overflow check before the write.\n\nSide note, emitting a warning splat with a backtrace might be overkill\nhere, but prefer not changing the behaviour other than not doing the\noverrun.\n\nDiscovered using AI-assisted static analysis confirmed by Intel Product\nSecurity.\n\n(cherry picked from commit 9284ab3b6e776c315883ac2611283d263c9460fd)"
              },
              "properties": {
