            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-68258",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: drm/amdkfd: Check bounds on CRIU restore queue type and mqd size"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndrm/amdkfd: Check bounds on CRIU restore queue type and mqd size\n\nWe weren't checking whether the values provided in the private\ndata in kfd CRIU restore were within bounds.\n\nFor queue type, add a KFD_QUEUE_TYPE_MAX and ensure the provided\ntype is less than it.\n\nFor mqd_size, add new function mqd_size_from_queue_type and confirm\nthat the provided mqd_size matches expectations.\n\n(cherry picked from commit f19d8086f6644083c913d70bfdeee20e1b6f46a5)"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-68258",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-68258\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-68258](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-68258)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndrm/amdkfd: Check bounds on CRIU restore queue type and mqd size\n\nWe weren't checking whether the values provided in the private\ndata in kfd CRIU restore were within bounds.\n\nFor queue type, add a KFD_QUEUE_TYPE_MAX and ensure the provided\ntype is less than it.\n\nFor mqd_size, add new function mqd_size_from_queue_type and confirm\nthat the provided mqd_size matches expectations.\n\n(cherry picked from commit f19d8086f6644083c913d70bfdeee20e1b6f46a5)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-68258**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-68258](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-68258)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndrm/amdkfd: Check bounds on CRIU restore queue type and mqd size\n\nWe weren't checking whether the values provided in the private\ndata in kfd CRIU restore were within bounds.\n\nFor queue type, add a KFD_QUEUE_TYPE_MAX and ensure the provided\ntype is less than it.\n\nFor mqd_size, add new function mqd_size_from_queue_type and confirm\nthat the provided mqd_size matches expectations.\n\n(cherry picked from commit f19d8086f6644083c913d70bfdeee20e1b6f46a5)"
              },
