            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-68267",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: drm/xe/rtp: Add RING_FORCE_TO_NONPRIV_DENY to OA whitelists"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndrm/xe/rtp: Add RING_FORCE_TO_NONPRIV_DENY to OA whitelists\n\nUnconditionally whitelisting OA registers is a security violation. Set\nRING_FORCE_TO_NONPRIV_DENY bit in OA nonpriv slots, so that OA registers\ndon't get whitelisted by default after probe, gt reset, resume and engine\nreset.\n\n(cherry picked from commit 90511bdcfda97211c01f1d945d4ea616578d8fca)"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-68267",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-68267\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: 6.12.105-1\nLink: [CVE-2026-68267](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-68267)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndrm/xe/rtp: Add RING_FORCE_TO_NONPRIV_DENY to OA whitelists\n\nUnconditionally whitelisting OA registers is a security violation. Set\nRING_FORCE_TO_NONPRIV_DENY bit in OA nonpriv slots, so that OA registers\ndon't get whitelisted by default after probe, gt reset, resume and engine\nreset.\n\n(cherry picked from commit 90511bdcfda97211c01f1d945d4ea616578d8fca)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-68267**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev|6.12.105-1|[CVE-2026-68267](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-68267)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndrm/xe/rtp: Add RING_FORCE_TO_NONPRIV_DENY to OA whitelists\n\nUnconditionally whitelisting OA registers is a security violation. Set\nRING_FORCE_TO_NONPRIV_DENY bit in OA nonpriv slots, so that OA registers\ndon't get whitelisted by default after probe, gt reset, resume and engine\nreset.\n\n(cherry picked from commit 90511bdcfda97211c01f1d945d4ea616578d8fca)"
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
