            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-68276",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: drm/amdgpu/gfx: fix cleaner shader IB buffer overflow"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndrm/amdgpu/gfx: fix cleaner shader IB buffer overflow\n\nThe cleaner shader sysfs path allocates a 16-dword (64 byte) IB but\nincorrectly fills (align_mask + 1) dwords. On GFX rings align_mask is\n0xff, so the loop wrote 256 dwords into a 64-byte buffer, causing a\nkernel page fault.\n\nThe IB only needs to be a minimal NOP shell to schedule the job; the\ncleaner shader itself is emitted on the ring via emit_cleaner_shader().\nFill 16 dwords to match the allocation.\n\nv2: Use ib_size_dw variable (Lijo)\n\n(cherry picked from commit bf21af331ebf72d0935fd70c73192414a422c03a)"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-68276",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-68276\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: 6.12.105-1\nLink: [CVE-2026-68276](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-68276)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndrm/amdgpu/gfx: fix cleaner shader IB buffer overflow\n\nThe cleaner shader sysfs path allocates a 16-dword (64 byte) IB but\nincorrectly fills (align_mask + 1) dwords. On GFX rings align_mask is\n0xff, so the loop wrote 256 dwords into a 64-byte buffer, causing a\nkernel page fault.\n\nThe IB only needs to be a minimal NOP shell to schedule the job; the\ncleaner shader itself is emitted on the ring via emit_cleaner_shader().\nFill 16 dwords to match the allocation.\n\nv2: Use ib_size_dw variable (Lijo)\n\n(cherry picked from commit bf21af331ebf72d0935fd70c73192414a422c03a)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-68276**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev|6.12.105-1|[CVE-2026-68276](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-68276)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndrm/amdgpu/gfx: fix cleaner shader IB buffer overflow\n\nThe cleaner shader sysfs path allocates a 16-dword (64 byte) IB but\nincorrectly fills (align_mask + 1) dwords. On GFX rings align_mask is\n0xff, so the loop wrote 256 dwords into a 64-byte buffer, causing a\nkernel page fault.\n\nThe IB only needs to be a minimal NOP shell to schedule the job; the\ncleaner shader itself is emitted on the ring via emit_cleaner_shader().\nFill 16 dwords to match the allocation.\n\nv2: Use ib_size_dw variable (Lijo)\n\n(cherry picked from commit bf21af331ebf72d0935fd70c73192414a422c03a)"
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
