            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-72365",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: netfs: Fix writethrough to use collection offload"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnetfs: Fix writethrough to use collection offload\n\nFix writethrough write to set NETFS_RREQ_OFFLOAD_COLLECTION on the request\nso that collection is processed asynchronously rather than only right at\nthe end - and also so that asynchronous O_SYNC writes get collected at all."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-72365",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-72365\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-72365](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-72365)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnetfs: Fix writethrough to use collection offload\n\nFix writethrough write to set NETFS_RREQ_OFFLOAD_COLLECTION on the request\nso that collection is processed asynchronously rather than only right at\nthe end - and also so that asynchronous O_SYNC writes get collected at all.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-72365**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-72365](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-72365)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnetfs: Fix writethrough to use collection offload\n\nFix writethrough write to set NETFS_RREQ_OFFLOAD_COLLECTION on the request\nso that collection is processed asynchronously rather than only right at\nthe end - and also so that asynchronous O_SYNC writes get collected at all."
              },
