            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-74444",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: drm/vmwgfx: validate DRAW_PRIMITIVES header size before division"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndrm/vmwgfx: validate DRAW_PRIMITIVES header size before division\n\nvmw_cmd_draw() computes\n\n\tmaxnum = (header-\u003esize - sizeof(cmd-\u003ebody)) / sizeof(*decl);\n\nwhere header-\u003esize is u32 and is taken straight from the user-supplied\ncommand stream.  When header-\u003esize is less than sizeof(cmd-\u003ebody) the\nunsigned subtraction wraps to nearly 4 GiB, producing a huge maxnum.\nAny user-controlled cmd-\u003ebody.numVertexDecls then passes the bound and\nthe loop dereferences decl[i] far past the end of the kernel command\nbounce buffer, producing an out-of-bounds read of kernel memory.\n\nReject undersized headers up front."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-74444",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-74444\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: 6.12.105-1\nLink: [CVE-2026-74444](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-74444)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndrm/vmwgfx: validate DRAW_PRIMITIVES header size before division\n\nvmw_cmd_draw() computes\n\n\tmaxnum = (header-\u003esize - sizeof(cmd-\u003ebody)) / sizeof(*decl);\n\nwhere header-\u003esize is u32 and is taken straight from the user-supplied\ncommand stream.  When header-\u003esize is less than sizeof(cmd-\u003ebody) the\nunsigned subtraction wraps to nearly 4 GiB, producing a huge maxnum.\nAny user-controlled cmd-\u003ebody.numVertexDecls then passes the bound and\nthe loop dereferences decl[i] far past the end of the kernel command\nbounce buffer, producing an out-of-bounds read of kernel memory.\n\nReject undersized headers up front.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-74444**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev|6.12.105-1|[CVE-2026-74444](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-74444)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndrm/vmwgfx: validate DRAW_PRIMITIVES header size before division\n\nvmw_cmd_draw() computes\n\n\tmaxnum = (header-\u003esize - sizeof(cmd-\u003ebody)) / sizeof(*decl);\n\nwhere header-\u003esize is u32 and is taken straight from the user-supplied\ncommand stream.  When header-\u003esize is less than sizeof(cmd-\u003ebody) the\nunsigned subtraction wraps to nearly 4 GiB, producing a huge maxnum.\nAny user-controlled cmd-\u003ebody.numVertexDecls then passes the bound and\nthe loop dereferences decl[i] far past the end of the kernel command\nbounce buffer, producing an out-of-bounds read of kernel memory.\n\nReject undersized headers up front."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
