            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-74455",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: can: peak_usb: validate uCAN receive record lengths"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ncan: peak_usb: validate uCAN receive record lengths\n\npcan_usb_fd_decode_buf() walks uCAN records packed in one USB\nreceive buffer.\n\nRequire each record to contain the fixed header for its type, and verify\nCAN payload bytes before copying them into the skb."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-74455",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-74455\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: 6.12.105-1\nLink: [CVE-2026-74455](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-74455)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ncan: peak_usb: validate uCAN receive record lengths\n\npcan_usb_fd_decode_buf() walks uCAN records packed in one USB\nreceive buffer.\n\nRequire each record to contain the fixed header for its type, and verify\nCAN payload bytes before copying them into the skb.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-74455**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev|6.12.105-1|[CVE-2026-74455](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-74455)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ncan: peak_usb: validate uCAN receive record lengths\n\npcan_usb_fd_decode_buf() walks uCAN records packed in one USB\nreceive buffer.\n\nRequire each record to contain the fixed header for its type, and verify\nCAN payload bytes before copying them into the skb."
