              "id": "CVE-2026-74532",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: Bluetooth: btintel: Validate length before parsing diagnostics TLV"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nBluetooth: btintel: Validate length before parsing diagnostics TLV\n\nbtintel_diagnostics() accesses tlv-\u003eval[0] without first validating\nthat the diagnostics VSE is long enough to contain that field, so\nmay cause reading data beyond the received frame.\n\nFix by validating the length before access."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-74532",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-74532\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: 6.12.105-1\nLink: [CVE-2026-74532](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-74532)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nBluetooth: btintel: Validate length before parsing diagnostics TLV\n\nbtintel_diagnostics() accesses tlv-\u003eval[0] without first validating\nthat the diagnostics VSE is long enough to contain that field, so\nmay cause reading data beyond the received frame.\n\nFix by validating the length before access.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-74532**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev|6.12.105-1|[CVE-2026-74532](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-74532)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nBluetooth: btintel: Validate length before parsing diagnostics TLV\n\nbtintel_diagnostics() accesses tlv-\u003eval[0] without first validating\nthat the diagnostics VSE is long enough to contain that field, so\nmay cause reading data beyond the received frame.\n\nFix by validating the length before access."
              },
