            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-74533",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: Bluetooth: ISO: fix race of kfree vs kref_get_unless_zero"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nBluetooth: ISO: fix race of kfree vs kref_get_unless_zero\n\nhci_conn::iso_data is accessed and modified without lock or RCU.\nThis leads to a race\n\n    [Task hdev-\u003eworkqueue]                 \t[Task 2]\n    iso_recv                                    iso_conn_put(conn)\n      conn = LOAD hcon-\u003eiso_data                  iso_conn_free(conn)\n      iso_conn_hold_unless_zero(conn)               hcon-\u003eiso_data = NULL\n                                                    kfree(conn)\n        kref_get_unless_zero(\u0026conn-\u003eref) /* UAF */\n\nand also to races in iso_conn_add() vs. iso_conn_free().\n\nFix by adding spinlock hci_conn::proto_lock and using it to guard\nhci_conn::iso_data."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-74533",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-74533\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-74533](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-74533)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nBluetooth: ISO: fix race of kfree vs kref_get_unless_zero\n\nhci_conn::iso_data is accessed and modified without lock or RCU.\nThis leads to a race\n\n    [Task hdev-\u003eworkqueue]                 \t[Task 2]\n    iso_recv                                    iso_conn_put(conn)\n      conn = LOAD hcon-\u003eiso_data                  iso_conn_free(conn)\n      iso_conn_hold_unless_zero(conn)               hcon-\u003eiso_data = NULL\n                                                    kfree(conn)\n        kref_get_unless_zero(\u0026conn-\u003eref) /* UAF */\n\nand also to races in iso_conn_add() vs. iso_conn_free().\n\nFix by adding spinlock hci_conn::proto_lock and using it to guard\nhci_conn::iso_data.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-74533**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-74533](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-74533)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nBluetooth: ISO: fix race of kfree vs kref_get_unless_zero\n\nhci_conn::iso_data is accessed and modified without lock or RCU.\nThis leads to a race\n\n    [Task hdev-\u003eworkqueue]                 \t[Task 2]\n    iso_recv                                    iso_conn_put(conn)\n      conn = LOAD hcon-\u003eiso_data                  iso_conn_free(conn)\n      iso_conn_hold_unless_zero(conn)               hcon-\u003eiso_data = NULL\n                                                    kfree(conn)\n        kref_get_unless_zero(\u0026conn-\u003eref) /* UAF */\n\nand also to races in iso_conn_add() vs. iso_conn_free().\n\nFix by adding spinlock hci_conn::proto_lock and using it to guard\nhci_conn::iso_data."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-74534",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: Bluetooth: ISO: fix refcounting of iso_conn"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nBluetooth: ISO: fix refcounting of iso_conn\n\niso_conn_del() and iso_chan_del() have a race that results to double-put\nof iso_conn:\n\n    [Task hdev-\u003eworkqueue]         [Task 2]\n    iso_conn_del                   iso_chan_del\n      iso_conn_hold_unless_zero      iso_conn_lock\n      iso_conn_lock                  conn-\u003esk = NULL\n                                     iso_conn_unlock\n      sk = iso_sock_hold(conn)  \u003c---------´\n      if (!sk) iso_conn_put          iso_conn_put\n      iso_conn_put /* UAF */\n\nThe extra put for !sk in iso_conn_del() is currently required since\nfailing iso_chan_add() may leave iso_conn not associated with any sk.\n\nFix by having iso_pi(sk)-\u003econn own refcount when non-NULL, so\niso_conn_del does not need to put it.  Adjust the iso_conn_add()\nrefcounting so that conn is put if it does not get associated with an\nsk."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-74534",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-74534\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-74534](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-74534)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nBluetooth: ISO: fix refcounting of iso_conn\n\niso_conn_del() and iso_chan_del() have a race that results to double-put\nof iso_conn:\n\n    [Task hdev-\u003eworkqueue]         [Task 2]\n    iso_conn_del                   iso_chan_del\n      iso_conn_hold_unless_zero      iso_conn_lock\n      iso_conn_lock                  conn-\u003esk = NULL\n                                     iso_conn_unlock\n      sk = iso_sock_hold(conn)  \u003c---------´\n      if (!sk) iso_conn_put          iso_conn_put\n      iso_conn_put /* UAF */\n\nThe extra put for !sk in iso_conn_del() is currently required since\nfailing iso_chan_add() may leave iso_conn not associated with any sk.\n\nFix by having iso_pi(sk)-\u003econn own refcount when non-NULL, so\niso_conn_del does not need to put it.  Adjust the iso_conn_add()\nrefcounting so that conn is put if it does not get associated with an\nsk.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-74534**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-74534](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-74534)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nBluetooth: ISO: fix refcounting of iso_conn\n\niso_conn_del() and iso_chan_del() have a race that results to double-put\nof iso_conn:\n\n    [Task hdev-\u003eworkqueue]         [Task 2]\n    iso_conn_del                   iso_chan_del\n      iso_conn_hold_unless_zero      iso_conn_lock\n      iso_conn_lock                  conn-\u003esk = NULL\n                                     iso_conn_unlock\n      sk = iso_sock_hold(conn)  \u003c---------´\n      if (!sk) iso_conn_put          iso_conn_put\n      iso_conn_put /* UAF */\n\nThe extra put for !sk in iso_conn_del() is currently required since\nfailing iso_chan_add() may leave iso_conn not associated with any sk.\n\nFix by having iso_pi(sk)-\u003econn own refcount when non-NULL, so\niso_conn_del does not need to put it.  Adjust the iso_conn_add()\nrefcounting so that conn is put if it does not get associated with an\nsk."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
