            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-74542",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: netfs: Fix folio_queue ENOMEM in writeback by adding a mempool"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnetfs: Fix folio_queue ENOMEM in writeback by adding a mempool\n\nFix the handling of folio_queue allocation failure in writeback by adding a\nmempool and passing in gfp_t flags to the rolling buffer functions that\nallocate memory, using the mempool if gfp != GFP_KERNEL.\n\nThis is then extended upwards and the gfp to be used for a request is stored\nin the netfs_io_request struct and is then used for both requests and\nsubrequests, eliminating the sleeping loops there.\n\nThe failure caused:\n\n    folio != NULL\n    WARNING: fs/netfs/write_issue.c:603 at netfs_writepages+0x883/0xa10 fs/netfs/write_issue.c:603, CPU#3: syz.0.17/5919"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-74542",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-74542\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-74542](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-74542)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnetfs: Fix folio_queue ENOMEM in writeback by adding a mempool\n\nFix the handling of folio_queue allocation failure in writeback by adding a\nmempool and passing in gfp_t flags to the rolling buffer functions that\nallocate memory, using the mempool if gfp != GFP_KERNEL.\n\nThis is then extended upwards and the gfp to be used for a request is stored\nin the netfs_io_request struct and is then used for both requests and\nsubrequests, eliminating the sleeping loops there.\n\nThe failure caused:\n\n    folio != NULL\n    WARNING: fs/netfs/write_issue.c:603 at netfs_writepages+0x883/0xa10 fs/netfs/write_issue.c:603, CPU#3: syz.0.17/5919",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-74542**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-74542](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-74542)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnetfs: Fix folio_queue ENOMEM in writeback by adding a mempool\n\nFix the handling of folio_queue allocation failure in writeback by adding a\nmempool and passing in gfp_t flags to the rolling buffer functions that\nallocate memory, using the mempool if gfp != GFP_KERNEL.\n\nThis is then extended upwards and the gfp to be used for a request is stored\nin the netfs_io_request struct and is then used for both requests and\nsubrequests, eliminating the sleeping loops there.\n\nThe failure caused:\n\n    folio != NULL\n    WARNING: fs/netfs/write_issue.c:603 at netfs_writepages+0x883/0xa10 fs/netfs/write_issue.c:603, CPU#3: syz.0.17/5919"
              },
