            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-74646",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: misc: fastrpc: take fl-\u003elock when moving mmaps on interrupted invoke"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nmisc: fastrpc: take fl-\u003elock when moving mmaps on interrupted invoke\n\nWhen an invoke is interrupted by a signal,\nwait_for_completion_interruptible() returns -ERESTARTSYS and\nfastrpc_internal_invoke() moves every buffer from fl-\u003emmaps onto\ncctx-\u003einvoke_interrupted_mmaps. This list_del()/list_add_tail() walk\nruns without holding fl-\u003elock, the lock that serialises fl-\u003emmaps in\nfastrpc_req_mmap() and fastrpc_req_munmap() everywhere else.\n\nTake fl-\u003elock around the move, matching every other fl-\u003emmaps accessor."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-74646",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-74646\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: 6.12.105-1\nLink: [CVE-2026-74646](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-74646)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nmisc: fastrpc: take fl-\u003elock when moving mmaps on interrupted invoke\n\nWhen an invoke is interrupted by a signal,\nwait_for_completion_interruptible() returns -ERESTARTSYS and\nfastrpc_internal_invoke() moves every buffer from fl-\u003emmaps onto\ncctx-\u003einvoke_interrupted_mmaps. This list_del()/list_add_tail() walk\nruns without holding fl-\u003elock, the lock that serialises fl-\u003emmaps in\nfastrpc_req_mmap() and fastrpc_req_munmap() everywhere else.\n\nTake fl-\u003elock around the move, matching every other fl-\u003emmaps accessor.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-74646**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev|6.12.105-1|[CVE-2026-74646](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-74646)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nmisc: fastrpc: take fl-\u003elock when moving mmaps on interrupted invoke\n\nWhen an invoke is interrupted by a signal,\nwait_for_completion_interruptible() returns -ERESTARTSYS and\nfastrpc_internal_invoke() moves every buffer from fl-\u003emmaps onto\ncctx-\u003einvoke_interrupted_mmaps. This list_del()/list_add_tail() walk\nruns without holding fl-\u003elock, the lock that serialises fl-\u003emmaps in\nfastrpc_req_mmap() and fastrpc_req_munmap() everywhere else.\n\nTake fl-\u003elock around the move, matching every other fl-\u003emmaps accessor."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
