            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-74675",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: vt: stabilize tty reference in kbd_keycode with tty_port_tty_get"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nvt: stabilize tty reference in kbd_keycode with tty_port_tty_get\n\nkbd_keycode() reads vc-\u003eport.tty without acquiring a tty reference,\nracing against con_shutdown() which clears port.tty under a different\nlock. Use tty_port_tty_get()/tty_kref_put() to hold a proper reference\nfor the duration the tty pointer is needed."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-74675",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-74675\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: 6.12.105-1\nLink: [CVE-2026-74675](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-74675)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nvt: stabilize tty reference in kbd_keycode with tty_port_tty_get\n\nkbd_keycode() reads vc-\u003eport.tty without acquiring a tty reference,\nracing against con_shutdown() which clears port.tty under a different\nlock. Use tty_port_tty_get()/tty_kref_put() to hold a proper reference\nfor the duration the tty pointer is needed.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-74675**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev|6.12.105-1|[CVE-2026-74675](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-74675)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nvt: stabilize tty reference in kbd_keycode with tty_port_tty_get\n\nkbd_keycode() reads vc-\u003eport.tty without acquiring a tty reference,\nracing against con_shutdown() which clears port.tty under a different\nlock. Use tty_port_tty_get()/tty_kref_put() to hold a proper reference\nfor the duration the tty pointer is needed."
              },
              "properties": {
