            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-74679",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: usb: gadget: f_ncm: Use unsigned int for ndp_index"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nusb: gadget: f_ncm: Use unsigned int for ndp_index\n\nThe variable ndp_index is declared as a signed integer, but it stores\nthe return value of get_ncm(), which is unsigned.\n\nA malicious host can supply a large offset that overflows the signed\nndp_index, making it negative. Because ndp_index is compared against\nunsigned bounds, this negative value bypasses sanity checks and leads\nto an out-of-bounds read when calculating the address of the NDP\nblock (ntb_ptr + ndp_index).\n\nFix this by changing ndp_index to unsigned int to ensure consistent\nunsigned comparisons throughout the function."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-74679",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-74679\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: 6.12.105-1\nLink: [CVE-2026-74679](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-74679)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nusb: gadget: f_ncm: Use unsigned int for ndp_index\n\nThe variable ndp_index is declared as a signed integer, but it stores\nthe return value of get_ncm(), which is unsigned.\n\nA malicious host can supply a large offset that overflows the signed\nndp_index, making it negative. Because ndp_index is compared against\nunsigned bounds, this negative value bypasses sanity checks and leads\nto an out-of-bounds read when calculating the address of the NDP\nblock (ntb_ptr + ndp_index).\n\nFix this by changing ndp_index to unsigned int to ensure consistent\nunsigned comparisons throughout the function.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-74679**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev|6.12.105-1|[CVE-2026-74679](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-74679)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nusb: gadget: f_ncm: Use unsigned int for ndp_index\n\nThe variable ndp_index is declared as a signed integer, but it stores\nthe return value of get_ncm(), which is unsigned.\n\nA malicious host can supply a large offset that overflows the signed\nndp_index, making it negative. Because ndp_index is compared against\nunsigned bounds, this negative value bypasses sanity checks and leads\nto an out-of-bounds read when calculating the address of the NDP\nblock (ntb_ptr + ndp_index).\n\nFix this by changing ndp_index to unsigned int to ensure consistent\nunsigned comparisons throughout the function."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
