            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-74704",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: net/sched: sch_cake: drop WARN_ON(1) for malformed packets in ACK filter"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnet/sched: sch_cake: drop WARN_ON(1) for malformed packets in ACK filter\n\nThe sch_cake ACK filter parses packets to find the TCP header and filter\nduplicated ACKs if the flow is backlogged. The parsing code contains a\nWARN_ON(1) which can be triggered by a malformed IP header in certain\ncases. Depending on the system configuration, this leads either to\neither spamming dmesg with warnings, or a panic if panic_on_warn is set.\n\nThe code already correctly skips the offending packet in the branch that\ntriggers the warning, so the WARN_ON itself doesn't really serve any\npurpose. So just drop it altogether to avoid the inconvenient side\neffects."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-74704",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-74704\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: 6.12.105-1\nLink: [CVE-2026-74704](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-74704)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnet/sched: sch_cake: drop WARN_ON(1) for malformed packets in ACK filter\n\nThe sch_cake ACK filter parses packets to find the TCP header and filter\nduplicated ACKs if the flow is backlogged. The parsing code contains a\nWARN_ON(1) which can be triggered by a malformed IP header in certain\ncases. Depending on the system configuration, this leads either to\neither spamming dmesg with warnings, or a panic if panic_on_warn is set.\n\nThe code already correctly skips the offending packet in the branch that\ntriggers the warning, so the WARN_ON itself doesn't really serve any\npurpose. So just drop it altogether to avoid the inconvenient side\neffects.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-74704**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev|6.12.105-1|[CVE-2026-74704](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-74704)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnet/sched: sch_cake: drop WARN_ON(1) for malformed packets in ACK filter\n\nThe sch_cake ACK filter parses packets to find the TCP header and filter\nduplicated ACKs if the flow is backlogged. The parsing code contains a\nWARN_ON(1) which can be triggered by a malformed IP header in certain\ncases. Depending on the system configuration, this leads either to\neither spamming dmesg with warnings, or a panic if panic_on_warn is set.\n\nThe code already correctly skips the offending packet in the branch that\ntriggers the warning, so the WARN_ON itself doesn't really serve any\npurpose. So just drop it altogether to avoid the inconvenient side\neffects."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-74705",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: udp: fix potential use-after-free in tunnel segmentation"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nudp: fix potential use-after-free in tunnel segmentation\n\n__skb_udp_tunnel_segment() gets the UDP header before ensuring the\ntunnel header is in the skb head. If the pull reallocates skb-\u003ehead,\nthe saved UDP header pointer is no longer valid.\n\nGet the UDP header after the pull to avoid a potential use-after-free."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-74705",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-74705\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: 6.12.105-1\nLink: [CVE-2026-74705](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-74705)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nudp: fix potential use-after-free in tunnel segmentation\n\n__skb_udp_tunnel_segment() gets the UDP header before ensuring the\ntunnel header is in the skb head. If the pull reallocates skb-\u003ehead,\nthe saved UDP header pointer is no longer valid.\n\nGet the UDP header after the pull to avoid a potential use-after-free.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-74705**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev|6.12.105-1|[CVE-2026-74705](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-74705)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nudp: fix potential use-after-free in tunnel segmentation\n\n__skb_udp_tunnel_segment() gets the UDP header before ensuring the\ntunnel header is in the skb head. If the pull reallocates skb-\u003ehead,\nthe saved UDP header pointer is no longer valid.\n\nGet the UDP header after the pull to avoid a potential use-after-free."
              },
