              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: secretly Monopolizing the CPU Without Superuser Privileges"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The process scheduler in the Linux kernel 2.6.16 gives preference to \"interactive\" processes that perform voluntary sleeps, which allows local users to cause a denial of service (CPU consumption), as described in \"Secretly Monopolizing the CPU Without Superuser Privileges.\""
              },
