            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-63999",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: ethtool: rss: fix indir_table and hkey leak on get_rxfh failure"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nethtool: rss: fix indir_table and hkey leak on get_rxfh failure\n\nrss_prepare_get() allocates the indirection table and hash key buffer\nvia rss_get_data_alloc(), then calls ops-\u003eget_rxfh() to populate them.\nIf get_rxfh() fails, the function returns an error without freeing\nthe allocation."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-63999",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-63999\nSeverity: LOW\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-63999](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-63999)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nethtool: rss: fix indir_table and hkey leak on get_rxfh failure\n\nrss_prepare_get() allocates the indirection table and hash key buffer\nvia rss_get_data_alloc(), then calls ops-\u003eget_rxfh() to populate them.\nIf get_rxfh() fails, the function returns an error without freeing\nthe allocation.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-63999**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|LOW|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-63999](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-63999)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nethtool: rss: fix indir_table and hkey leak on get_rxfh failure\n\nrss_prepare_get() allocates the indirection table and hash key buffer\nvia rss_get_data_alloc(), then calls ops-\u003eget_rxfh() to populate them.\nIf get_rxfh() fails, the function returns an error without freeing\nthe allocation."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "2.0",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "LOW"
                ]
              }
