            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-64060",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: netfs: Fix leak of request in netfs_write_begin() error handling"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnetfs: Fix leak of request in netfs_write_begin() error handling\n\nFix netfs_write_begin() to not leak our ref on the request in the event\nthat we get an error from netfs_wait_for_read()."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-64060",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-64060\nSeverity: LOW\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-64060](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-64060)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnetfs: Fix leak of request in netfs_write_begin() error handling\n\nFix netfs_write_begin() to not leak our ref on the request in the event\nthat we get an error from netfs_wait_for_read().",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-64060**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|LOW|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-64060](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-64060)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnetfs: Fix leak of request in netfs_write_begin() error handling\n\nFix netfs_write_begin() to not leak our ref on the request in the event\nthat we get an error from netfs_wait_for_read()."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "2.0",
                "tags": [
