            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-74644",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: mm/damon/ops-common: putback folios on invalid migrate nid"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nmm/damon/ops-common: putback folios on invalid migrate nid\n\ndamon_pa_migrate() and damos_va_migrate() isolate folios into a local list\nand then call damon_migrate_pages().  When target_nid is invalid\n(including the scheme default NUMA_NO_NODE / -1), damon_migrate_pages()\nreturns early without putting the folios back to the LRU.\n\nCallers then discard the list head while those folios remain isolated with\nan extra reference taken by folio_isolate_lru().  The pages stay off the\nLRU for as long as the mapping exists (anon active+inactive counts drop\nwhile RSS does not), and the leftover references can pin the pages after\nthe mapping is gone.\n\nPut the folios back on the invalid-nid path so ignored migration requests\nstill return them to the LRU."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-74644",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-74644\nSeverity: LOW\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: 6.12.105-1\nLink: [CVE-2026-74644](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-74644)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nmm/damon/ops-common: putback folios on invalid migrate nid\n\ndamon_pa_migrate() and damos_va_migrate() isolate folios into a local list\nand then call damon_migrate_pages().  When target_nid is invalid\n(including the scheme default NUMA_NO_NODE / -1), damon_migrate_pages()\nreturns early without putting the folios back to the LRU.\n\nCallers then discard the list head while those folios remain isolated with\nan extra reference taken by folio_isolate_lru().  The pages stay off the\nLRU for as long as the mapping exists (anon active+inactive counts drop\nwhile RSS does not), and the leftover references can pin the pages after\nthe mapping is gone.\n\nPut the folios back on the invalid-nid path so ignored migration requests\nstill return them to the LRU.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-74644**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|LOW|linux-libc-dev|6.12.105-1|[CVE-2026-74644](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-74644)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nmm/damon/ops-common: putback folios on invalid migrate nid\n\ndamon_pa_migrate() and damos_va_migrate() isolate folios into a local list\nand then call damon_migrate_pages().  When target_nid is invalid\n(including the scheme default NUMA_NO_NODE / -1), damon_migrate_pages()\nreturns early without putting the folios back to the LRU.\n\nCallers then discard the list head while those folios remain isolated with\nan extra reference taken by folio_isolate_lru().  The pages stay off the\nLRU for as long as the mapping exists (anon active+inactive counts drop\nwhile RSS does not), and the leftover references can pin the pages after\nthe mapping is gone.\n\nPut the folios back on the invalid-nid path so ignored migration requests\nstill return them to the LRU."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "2.0",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
