            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-80533",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:  x ..."
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nxfs: don't walk off the end of a null sc-\u003esa.agi_bp in AGI repair\n\nLOLLM noticed a longstanding bug where xrep_iunlink_walk_ondisk_bucket\ntries to walk ragi-\u003esc-\u003esa.agi_bp to rebuild the unlinked inode lists.\nUnfortunately, it's possible for agi_bp to be null if the buffer\nverifier fails, so we have to use ragi-\u003eagi_bp (which skips verifier\nchecks) instead."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-80533",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-80533\nSeverity: UNKNOWN\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: 6.12.105-1\nLink: [CVE-2026-80533](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-80533)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nxfs: don't walk off the end of a null sc-\u003esa.agi_bp in AGI repair\n\nLOLLM noticed a longstanding bug where xrep_iunlink_walk_ondisk_bucket\ntries to walk ragi-\u003esc-\u003esa.agi_bp to rebuild the unlinked inode lists.\nUnfortunately, it's possible for agi_bp to be null if the buffer\nverifier fails, so we have to use ragi-\u003eagi_bp (which skips verifier\nchecks) instead.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-80533**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|UNKNOWN|linux-libc-dev|6.12.105-1|[CVE-2026-80533](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-80533)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nxfs: don't walk off the end of a null sc-\u003esa.agi_bp in AGI repair\n\nLOLLM noticed a longstanding bug where xrep_iunlink_walk_ondisk_bucket\ntries to walk ragi-\u003esc-\u003esa.agi_bp to rebuild the unlinked inode lists.\nUnfortunately, it's possible for agi_bp to be null if the buffer\nverifier fails, so we have to use ragi-\u003eagi_bp (which skips verifier\nchecks) instead."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "0.0",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "UNKNOWN"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-80534",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:  x ..."
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nxfs: fix ilock leak on error in xfs_dq_get_next_id\n\nxfs_dq_get_next_id() takes the quota inode ILOCK before calling\nxfs_iread_extents().  If xfs_iread_extents() fails, the function returns\nimmediately without releasing the lock, leaking the quota inode ILOCK.\nThis can leave the quota inode locked and cause subsequent quota\noperations to hang.\n\nFix this by jumping to a common unlock path on error instead of returning\ndirectly."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-80534",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-80534\nSeverity: UNKNOWN\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: 6.12.105-1\nLink: [CVE-2026-80534](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-80534)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nxfs: fix ilock leak on error in xfs_dq_get_next_id\n\nxfs_dq_get_next_id() takes the quota inode ILOCK before calling\nxfs_iread_extents().  If xfs_iread_extents() fails, the function returns\nimmediately without releasing the lock, leaking the quota inode ILOCK.\nThis can leave the quota inode locked and cause subsequent quota\noperations to hang.\n\nFix this by jumping to a common unlock path on error instead of returning\ndirectly.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-80534**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|UNKNOWN|linux-libc-dev|6.12.105-1|[CVE-2026-80534](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-80534)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nxfs: fix ilock leak on error in xfs_dq_get_next_id\n\nxfs_dq_get_next_id() takes the quota inode ILOCK before calling\nxfs_iread_extents().  If xfs_iread_extents() fails, the function returns\nimmediately without releasing the lock, leaking the quota inode ILOCK.\nThis can leave the quota inode locked and cause subsequent quota\noperations to hang.\n\nFix this by jumping to a common unlock path on error instead of returning\ndirectly."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "0.0",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "UNKNOWN"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-80535",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:  x ..."
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nxfs: don't double-lock when deleting a self-referential directory\n\nLOLLM notices that the dirtree scrubber can detect a directory that\nrefers to itself.  In this case, it's not correct for the directory tree\nrepair code to try to iolock/ilock both sc-\u003eip and dp, because they're\nthe same inode.  Fix this by detecting that corner case and handling it\nappropriately."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-80535",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-80535\nSeverity: UNKNOWN\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: 6.12.105-1\nLink: [CVE-2026-80535](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-80535)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nxfs: don't double-lock when deleting a self-referential directory\n\nLOLLM notices that the dirtree scrubber can detect a directory that\nrefers to itself.  In this case, it's not correct for the directory tree\nrepair code to try to iolock/ilock both sc-\u003eip and dp, because they're\nthe same inode.  Fix this by detecting that corner case and handling it\nappropriately.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-80535**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|UNKNOWN|linux-libc-dev|6.12.105-1|[CVE-2026-80535](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-80535)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nxfs: don't double-lock when deleting a self-referential directory\n\nLOLLM notices that the dirtree scrubber can detect a directory that\nrefers to itself.  In this case, it's not correct for the directory tree\nrepair code to try to iolock/ilock both sc-\u003eip and dp, because they're\nthe same inode.  Fix this by detecting that corner case and handling it\nappropriately."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "0.0",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "UNKNOWN"
                ]
              }
