            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-80541",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:  d ..."
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndrm/amdgpu: validate GEM_CREATE domain combinations\n\nAMDGPU_GEM_CREATE checked domain bits against AMDGPU_GEM_DOMAIN_MASK,\nbut did not validate domain combinations. Userspace could combine\nCPU|GTT|VRAM with DOORBELL, GDS, GWS, or OA, making\namdgpu_bo_placement_from_domain() exceed AMDGPU_BO_MAX_PLACEMENTS and\nhit BUG_ON().\n\nAllow combinations only within CPU/GTT/VRAM, and require non-CPU/GTT/\nVRAM domains to be specified one at a time. Return -EINVAL for invalid\ncombinations in amdgpu_gem_create_ioctl().\n\nv2: Rename helper from amdgpu_gem_domain_valid() to\n    amdgpu_gem_are_domains_valid() (Christian)\n\n(cherry picked from commit db39852d0c39843cb02048dfb47e4b8c703e9080)"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-80541",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-80541\nSeverity: UNKNOWN\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: 6.12.105-1\nLink: [CVE-2026-80541](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-80541)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndrm/amdgpu: validate GEM_CREATE domain combinations\n\nAMDGPU_GEM_CREATE checked domain bits against AMDGPU_GEM_DOMAIN_MASK,\nbut did not validate domain combinations. Userspace could combine\nCPU|GTT|VRAM with DOORBELL, GDS, GWS, or OA, making\namdgpu_bo_placement_from_domain() exceed AMDGPU_BO_MAX_PLACEMENTS and\nhit BUG_ON().\n\nAllow combinations only within CPU/GTT/VRAM, and require non-CPU/GTT/\nVRAM domains to be specified one at a time. Return -EINVAL for invalid\ncombinations in amdgpu_gem_create_ioctl().\n\nv2: Rename helper from amdgpu_gem_domain_valid() to\n    amdgpu_gem_are_domains_valid() (Christian)\n\n(cherry picked from commit db39852d0c39843cb02048dfb47e4b8c703e9080)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-80541**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|UNKNOWN|linux-libc-dev|6.12.105-1|[CVE-2026-80541](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-80541)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndrm/amdgpu: validate GEM_CREATE domain combinations\n\nAMDGPU_GEM_CREATE checked domain bits against AMDGPU_GEM_DOMAIN_MASK,\nbut did not validate domain combinations. Userspace could combine\nCPU|GTT|VRAM with DOORBELL, GDS, GWS, or OA, making\namdgpu_bo_placement_from_domain() exceed AMDGPU_BO_MAX_PLACEMENTS and\nhit BUG_ON().\n\nAllow combinations only within CPU/GTT/VRAM, and require non-CPU/GTT/\nVRAM domains to be specified one at a time. Return -EINVAL for invalid\ncombinations in amdgpu_gem_create_ioctl().\n\nv2: Rename helper from amdgpu_gem_domain_valid() to\n    amdgpu_gem_are_domains_valid() (Christian)\n\n(cherry picked from commit db39852d0c39843cb02048dfb47e4b8c703e9080)"
              },
