            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-80607",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:  t ..."
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ntracing/probes: Remove WARN_ON_ONCE from parse_btf_arg\n\nSashiko found that user can cause this WARN_ON_ONCE() easily\nwith adding a kprobe event based on a raw address with BTF\nparameter.\n\nSince this is not an unexpected condition, remove the\nWARN_ON_ONCE()."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-80607",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-80607\nSeverity: UNKNOWN\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-80607](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-80607)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ntracing/probes: Remove WARN_ON_ONCE from parse_btf_arg\n\nSashiko found that user can cause this WARN_ON_ONCE() easily\nwith adding a kprobe event based on a raw address with BTF\nparameter.\n\nSince this is not an unexpected condition, remove the\nWARN_ON_ONCE().",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-80607**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|UNKNOWN|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-80607](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-80607)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ntracing/probes: Remove WARN_ON_ONCE from parse_btf_arg\n\nSashiko found that user can cause this WARN_ON_ONCE() easily\nwith adding a kprobe event based on a raw address with BTF\nparameter.\n\nSince this is not an unexpected condition, remove the\nWARN_ON_ONCE()."
              },
