            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-80614",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:  n ..."
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnet: emac: Fix NULL pointer dereference in emac_probe\n\nMove devm_request_irq() after devm_platform_ioremap_resource() so that\ndev-\u003eemacp is mapped before the interrupt handler can fire.  An early\ninterrupt hitting emac_irq() would dereference the NULL dev-\u003eemacp and\ncrash.\n\nAlso remove redundant error message. devm_platform_ioremap_resource()\nalready returns an error message with dev_err_probe()."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-80614",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-80614\nSeverity: UNKNOWN\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-80614](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-80614)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnet: emac: Fix NULL pointer dereference in emac_probe\n\nMove devm_request_irq() after devm_platform_ioremap_resource() so that\ndev-\u003eemacp is mapped before the interrupt handler can fire.  An early\ninterrupt hitting emac_irq() would dereference the NULL dev-\u003eemacp and\ncrash.\n\nAlso remove redundant error message. devm_platform_ioremap_resource()\nalready returns an error message with dev_err_probe().",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-80614**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|UNKNOWN|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-80614](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-80614)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnet: emac: Fix NULL pointer dereference in emac_probe\n\nMove devm_request_irq() after devm_platform_ioremap_resource() so that\ndev-\u003eemacp is mapped before the interrupt handler can fire.  An early\ninterrupt hitting emac_irq() would dereference the NULL dev-\u003eemacp and\ncrash.\n\nAlso remove redundant error message. devm_platform_ioremap_resource()\nalready returns an error message with dev_err_probe()."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "0.0",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "UNKNOWN"
                ]
              }
