            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-80616",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:  i ..."
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nieee802154: Avoid calling WARN_ON() on -ENOMEM in cfg802154_switch_netns()\n\nIt's pointless to call WARN_ON() in case of an allocation failure in\ndev_change_net_namespace() and device_rename(), since it only leads to\nuseless splats caused by deliberate fault injections, so avoid it.\n\nFound by Linux Verification Center (linuxtesting.org) with Syzkaller."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-80616",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-80616\nSeverity: UNKNOWN\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-80616](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-80616)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nieee802154: Avoid calling WARN_ON() on -ENOMEM in cfg802154_switch_netns()\n\nIt's pointless to call WARN_ON() in case of an allocation failure in\ndev_change_net_namespace() and device_rename(), since it only leads to\nuseless splats caused by deliberate fault injections, so avoid it.\n\nFound by Linux Verification Center (linuxtesting.org) with Syzkaller.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-80616**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|UNKNOWN|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-80616](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-80616)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nieee802154: Avoid calling WARN_ON() on -ENOMEM in cfg802154_switch_netns()\n\nIt's pointless to call WARN_ON() in case of an allocation failure in\ndev_change_net_namespace() and device_rename(), since it only leads to\nuseless splats caused by deliberate fault injections, so avoid it.\n\nFound by Linux Verification Center (linuxtesting.org) with Syzkaller."
              },
