            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-80679",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:  s ..."
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ns390/dasd: Fix potential NULL pointer dereference\n\ndasd_release_space() checks the implementation of the is_ese()\ndiscipline function before calling it to determine if a given device is\nan ESE DASD.\n\nThe current usage of the logical AND operator will lead to a NULL\npointer dereference as the function is called even if the function\npointer is NULL.\n\nFix this by using the logical OR operator."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-80679",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-80679\nSeverity: UNKNOWN\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: 6.12.105-1\nLink: [CVE-2026-80679](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-80679)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ns390/dasd: Fix potential NULL pointer dereference\n\ndasd_release_space() checks the implementation of the is_ese()\ndiscipline function before calling it to determine if a given device is\nan ESE DASD.\n\nThe current usage of the logical AND operator will lead to a NULL\npointer dereference as the function is called even if the function\npointer is NULL.\n\nFix this by using the logical OR operator.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-80679**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|UNKNOWN|linux-libc-dev|6.12.105-1|[CVE-2026-80679](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-80679)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ns390/dasd: Fix potential NULL pointer dereference\n\ndasd_release_space() checks the implementation of the is_ese()\ndiscipline function before calling it to determine if a given device is\nan ESE DASD.\n\nThe current usage of the logical AND operator will lead to a NULL\npointer dereference as the function is called even if the function\npointer is NULL.\n\nFix this by using the logical OR operator."
              },
