            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-80680",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:  i ..."
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ni2c: amd-mp2: Unregister callback on adapter add failure\n\namd_mp2_register_cb() stores the platform I2C context in the MP2 PCI\ndriver's callback table before the adapter is registered. If\ni2c_add_adapter() fails, probe returns and devres frees the context,\nbut the PCI driver can still dereference the stale pointer from its IRQ\nand system-sleep callbacks.\n\nUnregister the callback before returning the adapter registration error."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-80680",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-80680\nSeverity: UNKNOWN\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: 6.12.105-1\nLink: [CVE-2026-80680](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-80680)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ni2c: amd-mp2: Unregister callback on adapter add failure\n\namd_mp2_register_cb() stores the platform I2C context in the MP2 PCI\ndriver's callback table before the adapter is registered. If\ni2c_add_adapter() fails, probe returns and devres frees the context,\nbut the PCI driver can still dereference the stale pointer from its IRQ\nand system-sleep callbacks.\n\nUnregister the callback before returning the adapter registration error.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-80680**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|UNKNOWN|linux-libc-dev|6.12.105-1|[CVE-2026-80680](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-80680)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ni2c: amd-mp2: Unregister callback on adapter add failure\n\namd_mp2_register_cb() stores the platform I2C context in the MP2 PCI\ndriver's callback table before the adapter is registered. If\ni2c_add_adapter() fails, probe returns and devres frees the context,\nbut the PCI driver can still dereference the stale pointer from its IRQ\nand system-sleep callbacks.\n\nUnregister the callback before returning the adapter registration error."
              },
              "properties": {
