            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-80681",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:  v ..."
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nvxlan: re-fetch eth header after route_shortcircuit()\n\nBefore route_shortcircuit(), the eth header pointer is cached from eth_hdr(skb).\n\nInside route_shortcircuit(), pskb_may_pull() can be called, which may\nreallocate skb-\u003ehead.\n\nIn this case, returning to vxlan_xmit() leaves the cached eth pointer pointing to\nfreed memory, leading to a use-after-free when dereferencing eth-\u003eh_dest.\n\nFix this by updating eth = eth_hdr(skb) after calling route_shortcircuit()."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-80681",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-80681\nSeverity: UNKNOWN\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: 6.12.105-1\nLink: [CVE-2026-80681](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-80681)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nvxlan: re-fetch eth header after route_shortcircuit()\n\nBefore route_shortcircuit(), the eth header pointer is cached from eth_hdr(skb).\n\nInside route_shortcircuit(), pskb_may_pull() can be called, which may\nreallocate skb-\u003ehead.\n\nIn this case, returning to vxlan_xmit() leaves the cached eth pointer pointing to\nfreed memory, leading to a use-after-free when dereferencing eth-\u003eh_dest.\n\nFix this by updating eth = eth_hdr(skb) after calling route_shortcircuit().",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-80681**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|UNKNOWN|linux-libc-dev|6.12.105-1|[CVE-2026-80681](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-80681)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nvxlan: re-fetch eth header after route_shortcircuit()\n\nBefore route_shortcircuit(), the eth header pointer is cached from eth_hdr(skb).\n\nInside route_shortcircuit(), pskb_may_pull() can be called, which may\nreallocate skb-\u003ehead.\n\nIn this case, returning to vxlan_xmit() leaves the cached eth pointer pointing to\nfreed memory, leading to a use-after-free when dereferencing eth-\u003eh_dest.\n\nFix this by updating eth = eth_hdr(skb) after calling route_shortcircuit()."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "0.0",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
