            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-80684",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:  K ..."
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nKVM: s390: pci: Fix NULL dereference on AIBV allocation failure\n\nThe airq_iv_create() can return NULL on failure, but the return value was\nnever checked. If it fails, zdev-\u003eaibv will be NULL and fail when\ndereferenced in kvm_zpci_set_airq(). Add a NULL check and free the\npreviously allocated AISB bit and zdev-\u003eaisb on failure."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-80684",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-80684\nSeverity: UNKNOWN\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: 6.12.105-1\nLink: [CVE-2026-80684](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-80684)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nKVM: s390: pci: Fix NULL dereference on AIBV allocation failure\n\nThe airq_iv_create() can return NULL on failure, but the return value was\nnever checked. If it fails, zdev-\u003eaibv will be NULL and fail when\ndereferenced in kvm_zpci_set_airq(). Add a NULL check and free the\npreviously allocated AISB bit and zdev-\u003eaisb on failure.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-80684**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|UNKNOWN|linux-libc-dev|6.12.105-1|[CVE-2026-80684](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-80684)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nKVM: s390: pci: Fix NULL dereference on AIBV allocation failure\n\nThe airq_iv_create() can return NULL on failure, but the return value was\nnever checked. If it fails, zdev-\u003eaibv will be NULL and fail when\ndereferenced in kvm_zpci_set_airq(). Add a NULL check and free the\npreviously allocated AISB bit and zdev-\u003eaisb on failure."
              },
