            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-80691",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:  s ..."
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nscsi: target: iblock: Fix wrong PR ops NULL check for PREEMPT/RELEASE\n\nIn the iblock_execute_pr_out() function, PRO_PREEMPT,\nPRO_PREEMPT_AND_ABORT, and PRO_RELEASE all perform callback capability\nchecks through ops-\u003epr_clear. The error check allows unimplemented hooks\nto pass through the gate, resulting dereferencing a NULL function\npointer.\n\nCheck whether the hooks that need to be called are supported."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-80691",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-80691\nSeverity: UNKNOWN\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: 6.12.105-1\nLink: [CVE-2026-80691](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-80691)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nscsi: target: iblock: Fix wrong PR ops NULL check for PREEMPT/RELEASE\n\nIn the iblock_execute_pr_out() function, PRO_PREEMPT,\nPRO_PREEMPT_AND_ABORT, and PRO_RELEASE all perform callback capability\nchecks through ops-\u003epr_clear. The error check allows unimplemented hooks\nto pass through the gate, resulting dereferencing a NULL function\npointer.\n\nCheck whether the hooks that need to be called are supported.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-80691**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|UNKNOWN|linux-libc-dev|6.12.105-1|[CVE-2026-80691](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-80691)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nscsi: target: iblock: Fix wrong PR ops NULL check for PREEMPT/RELEASE\n\nIn the iblock_execute_pr_out() function, PRO_PREEMPT,\nPRO_PREEMPT_AND_ABORT, and PRO_RELEASE all perform callback capability\nchecks through ops-\u003epr_clear. The error check allows unimplemented hooks\nto pass through the gate, resulting dereferencing a NULL function\npointer.\n\nCheck whether the hooks that need to be called are supported."
