            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-56288",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "patch: GNU patch: Denial of Service via specially crafted patch file"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "GNU patch is vulnerable to a NULL pointer dereference when processing a specially crafted unified-diff patch file. Improper handling of consecutive end-of-file newline markers can corrupt internal hunk (single block of changes in diff) data structures, causing the application to pass a NULL pointer to fwrite() during patch processing.\nAn attacker can trigger this condition with a malicious patch file, causing the utility to crash and resulting in a denial of service.\n\n\n\nThis issue has been fixed in the commit e6d6a4e021660679d7fc9150f981d4920f722313"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-56288",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-56288\nSeverity: LOW\nPackage: patch\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-56288](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-56288)\nGNU patch is vulnerable to a NULL pointer dereference when processing a specially crafted unified-diff patch file. Improper handling of consecutive end-of-file newline markers can corrupt internal hunk (single block of changes in diff) data structures, causing the application to pass a NULL pointer to fwrite() during patch processing.\nAn attacker can trigger this condition with a malicious patch file, causing the utility to crash and resulting in a denial of service.\n\n\n\nThis issue has been fixed in the commit e6d6a4e021660679d7fc9150f981d4920f722313",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-56288**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|LOW|patch||[CVE-2026-56288](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-56288)|\n\nGNU patch is vulnerable to a NULL pointer dereference when processing a specially crafted unified-diff patch file. Improper handling of consecutive end-of-file newline markers can corrupt internal hunk (single block of changes in diff) data structures, causing the application to pass a NULL pointer to fwrite() during patch processing.\nAn attacker can trigger this condition with a malicious patch file, causing the utility to crash and resulting in a denial of service.\n\n\n\nThis issue has been fixed in the commit e6d6a4e021660679d7fc9150f981d4920f722313"
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "2.0",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "LOW"
                ]
              }
